  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Project Specifications**\n\nI\'m currently diving into the project requirements. I\'m focusing on the title and concept, which is a PWA for meal planning and shared grocery lists, ideal for two people who share meals. \"Specifica di Progetto: App Menu Settimanale & Spesa Condivisa\" provides the core framework.\n\n\n**Defining Key Features**\n\nNow, I\'m fleshing out the core functionality. I\'m prioritizing clear meal planning with immediate visibility, smart grocery list aggregation, seasonal recipe inspiration with anti-repetition rules, and real-time synchronization of shopping lists. User authentication and the shared household space are also being defined. I am exploring meal planning across two homes, distinguishing when to cook and shop separately.\n\n\n**Elaborating Shared Space Dynamics**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the \"Shared Space\" functionality. I\'m structuring user pairing via invitation codes (e.g., K9F2A1).  Once linked, both users will have equal permissions. Real-time synchronization is paramount, thinking of an Express backend with Server-Sent Events (SSE) for instant updates to menu and grocery list changes across devices connected via the shared code.\n\n**Structuring Meal Planning**\n\nI\'m dividing the weekly menu into lunch and dinner slots per day. I\'m planning dual fields, \"Together\" vs \"Separately,\" allowing each user to specify their meal situation. This setup will be customizable for each day\'s meals.\n\n\n**Refining Meal Selection**\n\nI\'m now focusing on meal selection details. I\'m thinking about individual and shared meals, with the option to specify \"Single Dish\" or \"Multiple Dishes\" for varying preferences within a meal. I also am planning to offer quick adding from a cookbook, seasonal suggestions with a single click, or fast free-text input. Weekly navigation, encompassing the current week, the next week, and an archive, is also being designed.\n\n\n**Developing Recipe Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating recipe features. I envision seasonal recipe suggestions (e.g., pumpkin in autumn). An \"Add to Menu\" button will insert the dish, automatically populating the grocery list with correctly labeled items. There will be the ability to save generated recipes to a personal cookbook, including season tags and conceptual ingredient lists.\n\nI\'m working on a dynamic grocery list. This will have conceptual checklists, no precise measurements. The automatic labeling system will tag items based on who is eating the meal, which could be *Together*, *Me* or *Partner*, with an option to manually add items as *Out of List*.\n\n\n**Organizing Grocery List Data**\n\nI\'m now focusing on grocery list organization. I\'m prioritizing sorting and filtering options: by department (Produce, Meat/Fish, Dairy, Pantry, Frozen, Household), and also by associated meal (e.g., *Lasagna: Mozzarella, Pasta, Sauce*). I will include sections for \"Other/Out of List\" items. Sorting by meal timing (Monday\'s ingredients before Thursday\'s) and assignees (*All*, *Together*, *My Items*, *Partner\'s Items*) will also be possible. Real-time checkboxes with strike-through and clean/reset buttons for completed items are also in development.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
