  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Package Dependencies**\n\nI\'m noting the crucial dependencies within `package.json`: `express`, `tsx`, and `dotenv`. I\'ve also re-familiarized myself with the established guideline: if the backend requires routes, a `server.ts` entry point is to be used, running Express, with `vite.middlewares` mounted in development. The command `\"dev\": \"tsx server.ts\"` will be used to run the server. I won\'t use this if backend isn\'t needed.\n\n\n**Integrating Deployment and Assets**\n\nI\'m now integrating deployment specifics. For full-stack applications, I\'ll set `\"start\": \"node server.ts\"` after building, and I need to remember to mount Express within `vite.config.ts`. I also made sure to confirm the lightweight libraries, `lucide-react` and `motion`, are present. Now I\'m checking the content of `metadata.json` and `index.html`. My first turn instructions have arrived: Set the name and description on the first turn. I need to make sure to update these with the information in `metadata.json`.\n\n\n\n**Defining Server Architecture**\n\nI\'m solidifying the full-stack structure. The server, built with Express, will utilize `vite.middlewares` during development and serve static files in production. It will listen on port 3000.  The data will be stored with in-memory households/shared spaces, backed up by a persistent JSON file (`data/households.json`).  Each household will contain unique codes, user data, and weekly menus. The weekly menus will include meal types for each meal.\n\n\n**Structuring Data Objects**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining data structures. I\'ve broken down `household` data, including arrays for `item`, `partnerDishes`, and an optional `notes` field. Then I\'m working with the shopping list, each with fields for `name`, `category`, `assignee`, and more. Lastly, I\'m defining a `recipes` library with fields like `season`, `ingredients`, and `prepTime`, all for Italian recipes!\n\n\n**Defining API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the API endpoints. I\'ve sketched out `/api/households/:code/events` for real-time updates and various RESTful endpoints for CRUD operations. I\'ve also added the Gemini AI endpoint for seasonal recipe suggestions, utilizing `@google/genai` with `gemini-3.8-flash`. I\'m detailing each endpoint\'s function and parameters.\n\n\n**Designing AI-Powered Endpoints**\n\nI\'m expanding the AI integration. I\'m focusing on two new endpoints. The first is `/api/ai/recipe-suggestions`, leveraging the Gemini AI with added parameters to refine the recipe generation. I\'ve considered fields like `recentDishes`, `userPreference` for dietary hints, ensuring the return of three seasonal Italian recipes, including name, description, season, prep time, and conceptual ingredient lists. The second endpoint, `POST /api/ai/categorize-product`, automatically detects supermarket departments for user-typed food or grocery terms.\n\n\n\n**Implementing User Preferences**\n\nI\'m now integrating user-specific preferences, focusing on the visual theme. I\'m storing the theme preference\342\200\224light, dark, or auto\342\200\224in `localStorage`. This will be per-device, ensuring each partner can personalize their view. I\'m considering avocado green and slate gray color options.\n\n\n**Refining Shopping List Views**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the shopping list interface. I\'m focusing on the assignee selector and how items can be viewed: by department, recipe affiliation, or temporal priority. There\'s also a filter for assignees. The design includes checkoff UX elements, such as tactile targets, strike-through text, and counters. I also need to incorporate the \"Remove checked\" function with an undo feature.\n\n\n**Reviewing Application Configuration**\n\nI\'m now diving into the current application configuration. I\'m examining the setup, starting with `package.json` and inspecting the `\"dev\"` script, now `\"vite --port=3000 --host=0.0.0.0\"`. I\'m also reviewing `server.ts` and `vite.config.ts` to ensure compatibility and the correct integration of backend with frontend, especially regarding Vite middlewares. I must integrate household functionality.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
