  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Server Configuration**\n\nI\'m currently reviewing the server configuration, focusing on the `package.json` file. Specifically, I\'m analyzing the scripts defined there: \"dev,\" \"build,\" \"preview,\" and \"clean.\" My goal is to understand how the Express backend is structured and managed through these scripts. I\'m taking note of the Vite configuration, especially the port and host settings, to understand how the application is intended to run.\n\n\n**Analyzing Server Initialization**\n\nI\'m now focusing on initializing the `server.ts` file. I\'ve noted the need to set up the GoogleGenAI instance, handling the API key and User-Agent in the headers. I\'m also examining how the households data will persist, which is a key part of the server setup, and I\'m looking at in-memory plus file-based persistence for Households, considering server restarts and data preservation via `./data/households.json`. I\'m going to look at adding Real-time Server-Sent Events (SSE) connections per household code now.\n\n\n**Defining Household Management**\n\nI\'m now thinking about household creation. I\'ve designed a household code system (e.g., `A8K2F9`). I\'ve also added the ability for users to join existing households. Finally, I\'m preloading initial data into a rich dataset. I\'m focusing on the first household with the code `AMORE1` and its default Italian recipes for the week. This will allow for testing and showcasing capabilities, providing a solid starting point for users and development.\n\n\n**Curating Recipe Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating detailed recipes and a corresponding shopping list for a sample household. I\'ve expanded the \"AMORE1\" household data to include a week\'s menu with specific Italian dishes, like spaghetti alle vongole and minestrone. The shopping list is conceptually categorized for ease of use, including items like \"Zucca mantovana\" and \"Spaghetti trafilati al bronzo.\" I\'ve also incorporated a library of over 16 Italian recipes, each tagged by season.\n\n\n**Defining API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now implementing the Gemini Flash API endpoints. The suggestions endpoint will receive the season, user preferences, and a list of previously cooked dishes to avoid repetition. It will return three seasonal recipe suggestions with details like name, description, season, preparation time, and ingredients. I\'m also creating the product categorization endpoint, which will categorize items into six predefined categories to enhance the shopping list functionality.\n\nAdditionally, I\'m checking the `package.json` scripts to update them for a full-stack structure. I\'ll test if `server.ts` runs with Vite middlewares in development, and if it correctly handles static files in production. Finally, I\'ll review the standard full-stack Vite + Express pattern using `createViteServer`.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_3346842"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false,\"Description\":\"Update dev and start scripts in package.json to run full-stack server\",\"EndLine\":12,\"Instruction\":\"Update package.json scripts for full-stack Express server\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"dev\\\": \\\"tsx server.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"vite build\\\",\\n    \\\"start\\\": \\\"tsx server.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"preview\\\": \\\"vite preview\\\",\\n    \\\"clean\\\": \\\"rm -rf dist server.js\\\",\\n    \\\"lint\\\": \\\"tsc --noEmit\\\"\\n  },\",\"StartLine\":6,\"TargetContent\":\"  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"dev\\\": \\\"vite --port=3000 --host=0.0.0.0\\\",\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"vite build\\\",\\n    \\\"preview\\\": \\\"vite preview\\\",\\n    \\\"clean\\\": \\\"rm -rf dist server.js\\\",\\n    \\\"lint\\\": \\\"tsc --noEmit\\\"\\n  },\",\"TargetFile\":\"/package.json\",\"toolAction\":\"Updating package.json scripts\",\"toolSummary\":\"Update dev and start scripts\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
