  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing User Interface**\n\nI\'m now diving into the user interface construction, specifically focusing on the header and navigation. The plan is to create a top header featuring the app brand, \"Menu & Spesa,\" a status indicator showing connection/sync (using a green dot or pulse for clarity), and an active user switcher. I\'m aiming for a clean and intuitive design for easy navigation.\n\n\n**Defining Navigation Components**\n\nI\'ve moved on to defining the navigation components. I\'m focusing on the structure of the bottom mobile bar and top desktop bar in `src/components/Navigation.tsx`. The weekly menu view is detailed in `src/components/WeeklyMenu/WeeklyMenuView.tsx`. This includes the week selector, day cards, and the logic for \"Insieme\" vs. \"Separati\" meal slot modes. I\'m considering multiple dishes per slot, catering to different dietary needs. I will include copy buttons for quick access to household codes.\n\n\n\n**Refining Shopping List Features**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the shopping list details, specifically in `src/components/ShoppingList/ShoppingListView.tsx`. I\'m focusing on the quick add bar with assignee selection and automatic category detection. I\'m also refining filter options, including by assignee and various grouping methods like department, meal, or temporal priority (Monday to Sunday). I\'m looking at clean checkboxes for items, with instant strikethrough and a display of who marked each item, along with a summary counter and \"remove checked\" functionality with confirmation.\n\n\n**Developing Recipe Library**\n\nI\'m now deep in the recipe library, specifically `src/components/Recipes/RecipesView.tsx`. I\'ve added seasonal filters (Autunno, Inverno, etc.) and a freshness score indicator (\360\237\237\242, \360\237\237\241). I\'m implementing a one-click \"Pianifica nel Menu\" feature with meal and day selection, seamlessly syncing ingredients to the shopping list. The \"Crea nuova ricetta\" form is also coming together.\n\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
