    session_summary: "{\"step_index\":1,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:52:03Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nQuesta \303\250 l\'idea di applicazione\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-17T02:52:03-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-w2op2gd7ig5avrhrpf6qqs-726438682148.europe-west2.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-w2op2gd7ig5avrhrpf6qqs-726438682148.europe-west2.run.app\\nUser Email: daniele.marra@buonarroti.tn.it\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\",\"media\":[{\"mime_type\":\"application/pdf\",\"uri\":\"meal_planner_design_spec.pdf\"}]}\n{\"step_index\":2,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:52:04Z\",\"input_tokens\":22055,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":666,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Project Goals**\\n\\nI\'ve begun examining the user\'s document, specifically focusing on the \\\"Specifica di Progetto\\\" PDF. It seems to detail an app for weekly menus and shared shopping lists. My initial assessment indicates the project is relevant to my skill set. I\'ve confirmed that the project\'s requirements appear to align well with my capabilities, particularly regarding the use of Gemini API, as evidenced in the provided document.\\n\\n\\n**Exploring AI Recipe Features**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the AI suggestions for recipe generation using the Gemini Flash API, considering seasonal ingredients and automated ingredient categorization. I have confirmed that the project leverages the `@google/genai: ^2.4.0` library. Also, I\'m analyzing the frontend design requirements for mobile-first, customizable UI themes, and the necessary PWA integration as specified. I\'m taking note of the Firebase and CloudSQL integration mentioned.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/skills/system_skills/gemini_api/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading Gemini API skill\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read Gemini API skill\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":4,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:52:11Z\",\"input_tokens\":18756,\"cache_read_tokens\":22286,\"output_tokens\":82,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"150\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Reading frontend design skill\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Read frontend design skill\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":6,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:52:14Z\",\"input_tokens\":2939,\"cache_read_tokens\":41039,\"output_tokens\":1883,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Project Specifications**\\n\\nI\'m currently diving into the project requirements. I\'m focusing on the title and concept, which is a PWA for meal planning and shared grocery lists, ideal for two people who share meals. \\\"Specifica di Progetto: App Menu Settimanale & Spesa Condivisa\\\" provides the core framework.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Key Features**\\n\\nNow, I\'m fleshing out the core functionality. I\'m prioritizing clear meal planning with immediate visibility, smart grocery list aggregation, seasonal recipe inspir\\n<truncated 2133 bytes>\\n. I\'m prioritizing sorting and filtering options: by department (Produce, Meat/Fish, Dairy, Pantry, Frozen, Household), and also by associated meal (e.g., *Lasagna: Mozzarella, Pasta, Sauce*). I will include sections for \\\"Other/Out of List\\\" items. Sorting by meal timing (Monday\'s ingredients before Thursday\'s) and assignees (*All*, *Together*, *My Items*, *Partner\'s Items*) will also be possible. Real-time checkboxes with strike-through and clean/reset buttons for completed items are also in development.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/package.json\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Inspecting package.json\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Inspect package.json\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":8,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:52:32Z\",\"input_tokens\":2612,\"cache_read_tokens\":44615,\"output_tokens\":2785,\"thinking\":\"**Observing Package Dependencies**\\n\\nI\'m noting the crucial dependencies within `package.json`: `express`, `tsx`, and `dotenv`. I\'ve also re-familiarized myself with the established guideline: if the backend requires routes, a `server.ts` entry point is to be used, running Express, with `vite.middlewares` mounted in development. The command `\\\"dev\\\": \\\"tsx server.ts\\\"` will be used to run the server. I won\'t use this if backend isn\'t needed.\\n\\n\\n**Integrating Deployment and Assets**\\n\\nI\'m now integrating deployment\\n<truncated 3043 bytes>\\nto incorporate the \\\"Remove checked\\\" function with an undo feature.\\n\\n\\n**Reviewing Application Configuration**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the current application configuration. I\'m examining the setup, starting with `package.json` and inspecting the `\\\"dev\\\"` script, now `\\\"vite --port=3000 --host=0.0.0.0\\\"`. I\'m also reviewing `server.ts` and `vite.config.ts` to ensure compatibility and the correct integration of backend with frontend, especially regarding Vite middlewares. I must integrate household functionality.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update metadata.json with app name and description\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"6\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Set name and description in metadata.json\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Menu & Spesa Condivisa\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"App PWA di pianificazione menu settimanale e lista della spesa condivisa per coppie con pasti insieme o separati, suggerimenti stagionali AI e sincronizzazione in tempo reale.\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"reques\\n<truncated 100 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"requestFramePermissions\\\\\\\": [],\\\\n  \\\\\\\"majorCapabilities\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\\\\\\\"]\\\\n}\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/metadata.json\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating metadata\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update metadata.json\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":10,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:52:58Z\",\"input_tokens\":3186,\"cache_read_tokens\":48056,\"output_tokens\":617,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update index.html with meta tags and app title\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"16\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Update index.html to match metadata.json and add PWA tags\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"    <title>Menu & Spesa Condivisa</title>\\\\n    <meta name=\\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"App PWA di pianificazione menu settimanale e lista della spesa condivisa per coppie con pasti insieme o separati, suggerimenti stagionali AI e sincronizzazione in tempo re\\n<truncated 1035 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"6\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\\\\n    <meta name=\\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\\\\\\\" />\\\\n    <meta property=\\\\\\\"og:title\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"My Google AI Studio App\\\\\\\" />\\\\n    <meta property=\\\\\\\"og:description\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"\\n<truncated 172 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/index.html\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating index.html\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update index.html\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":12,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:53:11Z\",\"input_tokens\":3478,\"cache_read_tokens\":49085,\"output_tokens\":333,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Menu & Spesa Condivisa\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"short_name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"MenuSpesa\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Pianificazione menu settimanale e lista della spesa condivisa per coppie.\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"start_url\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"display\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"standalone\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"background_color\\\\\\n<truncated 416 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create Web App Manifest for PWA compliance\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/manifest.json\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating manifest.json\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create PWA manifest\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":14,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:53:16Z\",\"input_tokens\":2573,\"cache_read_tokens\":50432,\"output_tokens\":253,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"// Simple Service Worker for offline PWA support\\\\nconst CACHE_NAME = \'menu-spesa-v1\';\\\\n\\\\nself.addEventListener(\'install\', (event) => {\\\\n  event.waitUntil(self.skipWaiting());\\\\n});\\\\n\\\\nself.addEventListener(\'activate\', (event) => {\\\\n  event.waitUntil(self.c\\n<truncated 353 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Basic Service Worker for PWA\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/sw.js\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating sw.js\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create service worker\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":16,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:53:23Z\",\"input_tokens\":2490,\"cache_read_tokens\":50877,\"output_tokens\":841,\"thinking\":\"**Generating Application Icons**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on generating application icons, specifically `/icon-192.png` and `/icon-512.png`. I\'m considering using an SVG canvas script for this, or potentially a lightweight svg-to-png generator. An alternative is crafting a nice SVG icon and a simple canvas generator. My immediate goal is a minimal script that creates a valid 192x192 icon.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"<svg xmlns=\\\\\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\\\\\" viewBox=\\\\\\\"0 0 512 512\\\\\\\" width=\\\\\\\"512\\\\\\\" height=\\\\\\\"512\\\\\\\">\\\\n  <defs>\\\\n    <linearGradient id=\\\\\\\"grad\\\\\\\" x1=\\\\\\\"0%\\\\\\\" y1=\\\\\\\"0%\\\\\\\" x2=\\\\\\\"100%\\\\\\\" y2=\\\\\\\"100%\\\\\\\">\\\\n      <stop offset=\\\\\\\"0%\\\\\\\" stop-color=\\\\\\\"#557A60\\\\\\\"/>\\\\n      <stop offset\\n<truncated 910 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create SVG icon for the app\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/icon.svg\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating icon.svg\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create app icon\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":18,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:53:31Z\",\"input_tokens\":3098,\"cache_read_tokens\":51314,\"output_tokens\":223,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Add favicon link in index.html\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"11\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add icon link in index.html\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"    <meta name=\\\\\\\"twitter:card\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"summary_large_image\\\\\\\" />\\\\n    <link rel=\\\\\\\"icon\\\\\\\" type=\\\\\\\"image/svg+xml\\\\\\\" href=\\\\\\\"/icon.svg\\\\\\\" />\\\\n    <meta name=\\\\\\\"theme-color\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"#557A60\\\\\\\" />\\\"\",\"StartLine\":\"9\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"    <meta name=\\\\\\\"twitter:card\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"summary_large_image\\\\\\\" />\\\\n    <meta name=\\\\\\\"theme-color\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"#557A60\\\\\\\" />\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/index.html\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Adding icon link\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Add favicon link\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":20,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:53:35Z\",\"input_tokens\":2718,\"cache_read_tokens\":52276,\"output_tokens\":1908,\"thinking\":\"**Examining Server Configuration**\\n\\nI\'m currently reviewing the server configuration, focusing on the `package.json` file. Specifically, I\'m analyzing the scripts defined there: \\\"dev,\\\" \\\"build,\\\" \\\"preview,\\\" and \\\"clean.\\\" My goal is to understand how the Express backend is structured and managed through these scripts. I\'m taking note of the Vite configuration, especially the port and host settings, to understand how the application is intended to run.\\n\\n\\n**Analyzing Server Initialization**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on i\\n<truncated 1766 bytes>\\n preparation time, and ingredients. I\'m also creating the product categorization endpoint, which will categorize items into six predefined categories to enhance the shopping list functionality.\\n\\nAdditionally, I\'m checking the `package.json` scripts to update them for a full-stack structure. I\'ll test if `server.ts` runs with Vite middlewares in development, and if it correctly handles static files in production. Finally, I\'ll review the standard full-stack Vite + Express pattern using `createViteServer`.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update dev and start scripts in package.json to run full-stack server\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"12\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Update package.json scripts for full-stack Express server\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"  \\\\\\\"scripts\\\\\\\": {\\\\n    \\\\\\\"dev\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"tsx server.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"build\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"vite build\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"start\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"tsx server.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"preview\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"vite preview\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"clean\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rm -rf dist server.js\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"lint\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"tsc --noEmit\\\\\\\"\\\\n  },\\\"\",\"StartLine\":\"6\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"  \\\\\\\"scripts\\\\\\\": {\\\\n    \\\\\\\"dev\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"vite --port=3000 --host=0.0.0.0\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"build\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"vite build\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"preview\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"vite preview\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"clean\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rm -rf dist server.js\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"lint\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"tsc --noEmit\\\\\\\"\\\\n  },\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/package.json\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating package.json scripts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update dev and start scripts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":22,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:53:49Z\",\"input_tokens\":2313,\"cache_read_tokens\":55501,\"output_tokens\":1717,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Initial Types**\\n\\nI\'m working on the initial TypeScript models. Right now, I\'m setting up a shared types file, `src/types.ts`. I\'ve already defined the `Season` and `DepartmentCategory` types, including the `\'ortofrutta\'` category. Next, I need to flesh out more of the data models based on these fundamental types.\\n\\n\\n**Expanding Core Types**\\n\\nI\'ve expanded the `DepartmentCategory` type to include `\'macelleria_pescheria\'`, `\'latticini_freschi\'`, `\'dispensa_secco\'`, `\'surgelati\'`, and `\'cura_casa_alt\\n<truncated 253 bytes>\\ne these interfaces are comprehensive and flexible.\\n\\n\\n**Defining More Types**\\n\\nI\'m now defining the `Recipe`, `UserProfile`, and `Household` types. I\'m focusing on attributes like `createdAt`, `prepTime`, and the structure of `ingredients` within `Recipe`. I\'m also including `lastPreparedDate` as an optional attribute. The `UserProfile` includes role and theme settings. Finally, I\'m fleshing out `Household` with properties for managing menus, the shopping list, and recipes, including an `updatedAt` field.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"export type Season = \'spring\' | \'summer\' | \'autumn\' | \'winter\' | \'all_year\';\\\\n\\\\nexport type DepartmentCategory =\\\\n  | \'ortofrutta\'\\\\n  | \'macelleria_pescheria\'\\\\n  | \'latticini_freschi\'\\\\n  | \'dispensa_secco\'\\\\n  | \'surgelati\'\\\\n  | \'cura_casa_altro\';\\\\n\\\\nexpor\\n<truncated 2159 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Shared TypeScript types for Household, Week Menu, Shopping List, and Recipes\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/types.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing shared types\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create src/types.ts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":24,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:54:02Z\",\"input_tokens\":4052,\"cache_read_tokens\":55909,\"output_tokens\":6299,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Seed Data**\\n\\nOkay, I\'m working on the initial data and utility functions. I\'ve taken a look at `src/data/initialData.ts`. I\'m figuring out how to get the current season based on the month, with October kicking off Autumn, or Autunno if you prefer. Then, I\'m figuring out how to calculate the current week ID, which will look something like `2026-W42`.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Initial Data Structures**\\n\\nI\'ve been defining the structure for the default household data, including code `CASA01` and templates for new households. I\'ve also populated a rich set of 18 Italian recipes, categorized by season, including Autumn, Winter, Spring, Summer, and Year-Round options. I am also working on an initial weekly menu with lunch and dinner slots for \\\"Insieme\\\" and \\\"Separati\\\" options. Finally, I will be working on the initial shopping list data.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import { Household, Recipe, WeekMenu, Season } from \'../types.ts\';\\\\n\\\\nexport const DEPARTMENT_LABELS: Record<string, { label: string; icon: string; order: number }> = {\\\\n  ortofrutta: { label: \'Ortofrutta\', icon: \'\360\237\245\225\', order: 1 },\\\\n  macelleria_pescheri\\n<truncated 17111 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Initial default datasets, recipes, seed week menu and helper functions\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/data/initialData.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating seed data\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create initialData.ts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":26,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:54:43Z\",\"input_tokens\":6686,\"cache_read_tokens\":59896,\"output_tokens\":6274,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Server.ts**\\n\\nI\'m now focused on building `server.ts`. It looks like I\'ll need to import `express`, `vite`\'s `createServer`, `path`, and `fs` modules for this implementation.\\n\\n\\n**Adding Imports and Config**\\n\\nI\'ve added several imports, including `fileURLToPath` from \'url\', and `dotenv` to load environment variables. I\'m configuring the GoogleGenAI instance with the API key from `.env` and setting a \'User-Agent\' header. I\'m also now planning for file storage in `./data/households.json`. I\'m starting to build out a system of SSE clients per household code.\\n\\n\\n**Defining API Endpoints**\\n\\nI\'m now outlining the API endpoints. I\'m focusing on POST requests for adding, deleting, and clearing shopping list items, and also for menu updates and recipe management. I\'ve also defined the SSE subscription endpoint for real-time updates, including headers for content type, cache control, and connection management, and initial event signaling. The endpoints for Gemini Flash AI have also been conceptualized.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import express, { Request, Response } from \'express\';\\\\nimport { createServer as createViteServer } from \'vite\';\\\\nimport path from \'path\';\\\\nimport fs from \'fs\';\\\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \'url\';\\\\nimport dotenv from \'dotenv\';\\\\nimport { GoogleGenAI, Type\\n<truncated 17556 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Express server with real-time SSE, Gemini Flash AI integrations, and Household storage\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/server.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating server.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create server.ts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":28,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:55:33Z\",\"input_tokens\":6652,\"cache_read_tokens\":66551,\"output_tokens\":2441,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing CSS Styling**\\n\\nI\'m currently examining the `src/index.css` file to understand the existing styling. My focus is on how the application handles theming, particularly concerning light, dark, and auto modes. I\'m looking for clues on how color palettes are implemented to align with the user\'s specified preferences.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"@import \\\\\\\"tailwindcss\\\\\\\";\\\\n\\\\n:root {\\\\n  font-family: \'Plus Jakarta Sans\', system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, sans-serif;\\\\n  -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent;\\\\n\\\\n  /* Salvia (Default) */\\\\n  -\\n<truncated 4185 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Theme definitions, color palettes (Salvia, Terracotta, Mirtillo, Avocado, Slate) and dark mode rules\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/index.css\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Styling themes and typography\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update index.css\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":30,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:55:57Z\",\"input_tokens\":2664,\"cache_read_tokens\":73161,\"output_tokens\":6014,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Frontend Components**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the frontend implementation. Currently, my focus is on laying out the core components and hooks. I\'ve started by defining `HouseholdContext.tsx`, which will manage the household state, current role, and preferences. I\'m aiming for a clean separation of concerns and clear data flow from the outset. I am still considering what additional information will be stored in `HouseholdContext.tsx`.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Context Data**\\n\\nI\'ve been working on fleshing out the `HouseholdContext` data structure. I\'ve added color themes, display modes, a household code stored in local storage, and a real-time SSE listener. I\'m now listing all the various actions, including functions for managing shopping items, meal slots, and recipes. I have also added state variables that manage online status and the current week.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { createContext, useContext, useState, useEffect, useCallback, useMemo } from \'react\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Household,\\\\n  ShoppingItem,\\\\n  Recipe,\\\\n  ColorTheme,\\\\n  DisplayMode,\\\\n  DayKey,\\\\n  MealType,\\\\n  MealSlot,\\\\n  Dish,\\\\n  MealSlotType,\\\\n  Assig\\n<truncated 19942 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Household context providing real-time sync, state management, and actions\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/context/HouseholdContext.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating Household context\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create HouseholdContext.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":32,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:56:32Z\",\"input_tokens\":6377,\"cache_read_tokens\":75756,\"output_tokens\":3569,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing User Interface**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the user interface construction, specifically focusing on the header and navigation. The plan is to create a top header featuring the app brand, \\\"Menu & Spesa,\\\" a status indicator showing connection/sync (using a green dot or pulse for clarity), and an active user switcher. I\'m aiming for a clean and intuitive design for easy navigation.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Navigation Components**\\n\\nI\'ve moved on to defining the navigation components. I\'m focusing on the structur\\n<truncated 913 bytes>\\nh item, along with a summary counter and \\\"remove checked\\\" functionality with confirmation.\\n\\n\\n**Developing Recipe Library**\\n\\nI\'m now deep in the recipe library, specifically `src/components/Recipes/RecipesView.tsx`. I\'ve added seasonal filters (Autunno, Inverno, etc.) and a freshness score indicator (\360\237\237\242, \360\237\237\241). I\'m implementing a one-click \\\"Pianifica nel Menu\\\" feature with meal and day selection, seamlessly syncing ingredients to the shopping list. The \\\"Crea nuova ricetta\\\" form is also coming together.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React from \'react\';\\\\nimport { Calendar, ShoppingCart, BookOpen, Settings, Users, Sparkles, RefreshCw } from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { useHousehold } from \'../context/HouseholdContext.tsx\';\\\\n\\\\nexport type TabType = \'menu\' | \'shopping\' | \'recipes\' | \\n<truncated 8607 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Navigation header and responsive desktop/mobile bottom bars\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/Navigation.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating Navigation component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create Navigation.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":34,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:57:00Z\",\"input_tokens\":3848,\"cache_read_tokens\":82389,\"output_tokens\":3520,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Component Specs**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on outlining the `WeeklyMenu` component. I\'m carefully reviewing the specification to understand the specific feature requirements for the \\\"Menu Settiman\\\" functionality. I\'m breaking down the task into smaller, manageable subcomponents within `src/components/WeeklyMenu`.\\n\\n\\n**Designing the `AddDishModal`**\\n\\nI\'ve moved on to designing the `AddDishModal`. My focus is on facilitating quick and intuitive dish selection. I\'m incorporating options for custom entries, recipe selection (including freshness status), and automatic ingredient addition to the shopping list. The target selector is also essential. I\'m planning the development of `src/components/WeeklyMenu/AddDishModal.tsx` next.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { X, Plus, Sparkles, BookOpen, Clock, Check } from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { useHousehold } from \'../../context/HouseholdContext.tsx\';\\\\nimport { Recipe, DayKey, MealType } from \'../../types.ts\';\\\\nimport { S\\n<truncated 12110 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Modal to add custom dishes or choose from personal recipes with freshness indicator and auto-shopping sync\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/WeeklyMenu/AddDishModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating AddDishModal component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create AddDishModal.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":36,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:57:23Z\",\"input_tokens\":3802,\"cache_read_tokens\":86228,\"output_tokens\":4684,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Weekly Menu View**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the construction of `WeeklyMenuView.tsx`. My current focus is nailing down the features. I need week navigation: prev/current/next week buttons, plus a \\\"Back to this week\\\" button. I also have to implement days Monday to Sunday with appropriate Italian translations. Each day will have associated content that I\'ll need to define.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  ChevronLeft,\\\\n  ChevronRight,\\\\n  Plus,\\\\n  Trash2,\\\\n  Users,\\\\n  User,\\\\n  Sparkles,\\\\n  ShoppingBag,\\\\n  RotateCcw,\\\\n  CalendarDays,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { useHousehold } from \'../../context/Hou\\n<truncated 15729 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"WeeklyMenuView component for Monday to Sunday meal planning with together/separate toggles\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/WeeklyMenu/WeeklyMenuView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating WeeklyMenuView component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create WeeklyMenuView.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":38,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:57:51Z\",\"input_tokens\":5007,\"cache_read_tokens\":89907,\"output_tokens\":6552,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Shopping List**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into building the ShoppingList view component, `ShoppingListView.tsx`. I\'m meticulously verifying its features based on the provided specifications, specifically focusing on the dynamic checklist nature as described in the PDF, for example, Pasta and Passata di Pomodoro. This approach ensures it meets the criteria.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Item Assignment**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on automatic item labeling based on meal assignments. I\'m implementing logic to tag items as \'Insieme,\' \'Daniele,\' or \'Partner\' based on the specified meal scenario. Manual items require user-defined labels. I\'ve also incorporated sorting and filtering options for efficient list management, including sections like Ortofrutta and Piatto d\'Appartenenza. Priority-based sorting by day is also under development.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState, useMemo } from \'react\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Check,\\\\n  Plus,\\\\n  Trash2,\\\\n  Filter,\\\\n  CheckCircle2,\\\\n  Layers,\\\\n  Calendar,\\\\n  Utensils,\\\\n  Tag,\\\\n  Sparkles,\\\\n  ShoppingBag,\\\\n  RotateCcw,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { useHousehold } \\n<truncated 21544 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"ShoppingListView component with live grocery checklist, department/recipe/day grouping, assignee filtering and auto-categorization\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/ShoppingList/ShoppingListView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating ShoppingListView component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create ShoppingListView.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":40,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:58:30Z\",\"input_tokens\":6944,\"cache_read_tokens\":94812,\"output_tokens\":5229,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Components Now**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into building the `RecipesView.tsx` and the `AISuggestModal.tsx` components. Currently, I\'m reviewing Section 2.3 for specifications on the hybrid and seasonal dish suggestion engine, which will dictate the AI\'s functionality. My focus is on the integration of this AI suggestion feature and how it is laid out in the component and drawer.\\n\\n\\n**Designing the Suggestion Modal**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on designing the `AISuggestModal.tsx` component. This involves displaying a seasonal banner and allowing user selection of both the season and a culinary hint or mood. I\'m aiming for a straightforward user interface that supports seasonal ingredient suggestions.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Sparkles,\\\\n  X,\\\\n  Clock,\\\\n  Check,\\\\n  ShoppingBag,\\\\n  Plus,\\\\n  BookOpen,\\\\n  Calendar,\\\\n  Flame,\\\\n  Loader2,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { useHousehold } from \'../../context/HouseholdContext.tsx\';\\\\\\n<truncated 17548 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"AISuggestModal component connecting to Gemini Flash for seasonal recipe generation with anti-repetition rules and 1-click menu/shopping creation\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/Recipes/AISuggestModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating AISuggestModal component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create AISuggestModal.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":42,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:59:02Z\",\"input_tokens\":5565,\"cache_read_tokens\":101686,\"output_tokens\":6828,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing RecipesView.tsx**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on building `src/components/Recipes/RecipesView.tsx`. My current focus involves implementing the display of a user\'s recipe archive, adding search functionality by recipe name or ingredient, and integrating season filter tabs (Tutto, Autunno, Inverno, Primavera, Estate, Tutto l\'anno). I\'ll also add a freshness status feature to the display.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState, useMemo } from \'react\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  BookOpen,\\\\n  Plus,\\\\n  Sparkles,\\\\n  Search,\\\\n  Clock,\\\\n  Calendar,\\\\n  ShoppingBag,\\\\n  Check,\\\\n  Utensils,\\\\n  ChevronRight,\\\\n  Flame,\\\\n  X,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { useHousehold } from \\n<truncated 25881 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"RecipesView component with personal recipe archive, freshness tracking, season filtering and 1-click weekly planning\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/Recipes/RecipesView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating RecipesView component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create RecipesView.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":44,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T09:59:40Z\",\"input_tokens\":7213,\"cache_read_tokens\":107073,\"output_tokens\":6892,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Settings & Household**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on building the Settings and Household Space View, specifically `src/components/Settings/SettingsView.tsx`. I\'m starting by considering the necessary components, particularly around authentication and the shared household space features. Rapid login via Google or user profile is the initial point of focus.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Shared Space & Theme**\\n\\nI\'ve been defining the shared space functionality. The initial user will create the \\\"Shared Space\\\" and generate an invite link or a six-digit code. The second user enters this, and the accounts are permanently linked. Both have full read/write permissions for recipes, menus, and shopping lists. I\'m also planning theme customization. I\'ll offer Light, Dark, or Auto modes, and include multiple color palettes. The user\'s preferences will be saved locally and synced for individual theme choices.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Users,\\\\n  Copy,\\\\n  Check,\\\\n  Palette,\\\\n  Sun,\\\\n  Moon,\\\\n  Laptop,\\\\n  Share2,\\\\n  UserCheck,\\\\n  Home,\\\\n  PlusCircle,\\\\n  KeyRound,\\\\n  Sparkles,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { useHousehold } from \'../..\\n<truncated 24615 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"SettingsView component for household sharing code, invitation link, user profiles and theme/color selection\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/Settings/SettingsView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating SettingsView component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create SettingsView.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":46,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T10:00:19Z\",\"input_tokens\":7274,\"cache_read_tokens\":114202,\"output_tokens\":953,\"thinking\":\"**Integrating the Pieces**\\n\\nI\'m now integrating the different components into `src/App.tsx`. The application will be wrapped in `HouseholdProvider`. I\'ve set up the main container with the active tab switcher. Also, I\'ve got the global `AISuggestModal` ready, which can be triggered from anywhere in the app.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"/**\\\\n * @license\\\\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\\\\n */\\\\n\\\\nimport React, { useState, useEffect } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { HouseholdProvider, useHousehold } from \'./context/HouseholdContext.tsx\';\\\\nimport { Navigation, TabType } from \'./components/Navi\\n<truncated 2524 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"App.tsx entry point with HouseholdProvider, URL parameter join handler, tabs, and global AI modal\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update App.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":48,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T10:00:27Z\",\"input_tokens\":3239,\"cache_read_tokens\":119373,\"output_tokens\":71,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"lint_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking code for TypeScript errors\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Run lint_applet\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":50,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T10:00:31Z\",\"input_tokens\":2314,\"cache_read_tokens\":120470,\"output_tokens\":64,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Testing applet compilation\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Run compile_applet\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":52,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T10:00:35Z\",\"input_tokens\":2287,\"cache_read_tokens\":120643,\"output_tokens\":81,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"restart_dev_server\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Restarting dev server to launch full-stack Express server\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Restart dev server\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":54,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T10:00:39Z\",\"input_tokens\":2301,\"cache_read_tokens\":120789,\"output_tokens\":101,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"curl -s http://localhost:3000/api/households/CASA01 | head -c 200\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"5000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Verifying API endpoint\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Test household API\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":56,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T10:00:44Z\",\"input_tokens\":2402,\"cache_read_tokens\":120946,\"output_tokens\":134,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"run_command\",\"args\":{\"CommandLine\":\"\\\"curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/ai/suggest-seasonal -H \\\\\\\"Content-Type: application/json\\\\\\\" -d \'{\\\\\\\"season\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"autumn\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"recentDishes\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Risotto alla Zucca\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"preferences\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"veloce\\\\\\\"}\' | head -c 250\\\"\",\"Cwd\":\"\\\"/\\\"\",\"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":\"10000\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Testing AI endpoint\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Test Gemini suggest endpoint\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":58,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T10:00:57Z\",\"input_tokens\":2439,\"cache_read_tokens\":121203,\"output_tokens\":84,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"manage_task\",\"args\":{\"Action\":\"\\\"status\\\"\",\"TaskId\":\"\\\"cdd35663-1681-4cae-907e-a5de32ff2712/task-57\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking task status\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check task status\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":60,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T10:00:59Z\",\"input_tokens\":2349,\"cache_read_tokens\":121500,\"output_tokens\":94,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"schedule\",\"args\":{\"DurationSeconds\":\"3\",\"Prompt\":\"\\\"Check Gemini response\\\"\",\"TimerCondition\":\"\\\"cdd35663-1681-4cae-907e-a5de32ff2712/task-57\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Scheduling check\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Schedule check\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":62,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T10:01:02Z\",\"input_tokens\":2339,\"cache_read_tokens\":121708,\"output_tokens\":557,\"content\":\"A background task update was received:\\nTaskId: cdd35663-1681-4cae-907e-a5de32ff2712/task-57\\nExitCode: 0\\nMessage: Task completed with exit code 0.\\nLog:\\n{\\\"success\\\":true,\\\"recipes\\\":[{\\\"category\\\":\\\"Primo\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Un primo piatto autunnale cremoso e profumato, perfetto per una cena veloce senza rinunciare al sapore.\\\",\\\"ingredients\\\":[\\\"Tagliatelle all\'uovo\\\",\\\"Funghi champignon e porcini\\\",\\\"Panna fresca\\\",\\\"Prezzemolo fresco\\\",\\\"Aglio\\\",\\\"Olio EVO\\\"],\\\"name\\\":\\\"Tagliatelle cremose ai Funghi e Timo\\\",\\\"prepTime\\\":\\\"20 min\\\",\\\"seas\\n<truncated 475 bytes>\\nchi sono ortaggi e frutti autunnali freschissimi e ricchi di vitamine.\\\"},{\\\"category\\\":\\\"Piatto Unico\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Una frittata rustica e sostanziosa, ideale come piatto unico caldo e confortevole.\\\",\\\"ingredients\\\":[\\\"Uova fresche\\\",\\\"Radicchio rosso tardivo\\\",\\\"Provola affumicata\\\",\\\"Cipolla rossa\\\",\\\"Olio EVO\\\"],\\\"name\\\":\\\"Frittata rustica con Radicchio Rosso e Provola affumicata\\\",\\\"prepTime\\\":\\\"20 min\\\",\\\"season\\\":\\\"autumn\\\",\\\"whySeasonal\\\":\\\"Il radicchio rosso tardivo trova in autunno la sua massima croccantezza e dolcezza.\\\"}]}\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"manage_task\",\"args\":{\"Action\":\"\\\"kill\\\"\",\"TaskId\":\"\\\"cdd35663-1681-4cae-907e-a5de32ff2712/task-61\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Cleaning up timer task\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Kill timer task\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n{\"step_index\":65,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T10:01:08Z\",\"input_tokens\":3050,\"cache_read_tokens\":121883,\"output_tokens\":951,\"content\":\"L\'applicazione **Menu Settimanale & Spesa Condivisa (PWA)** \303\250 stata realizzata seguendo in ogni dettaglio le specifiche tecniche e funzionali del documento.\\n\\n### \360\237\214\237 Funzionalit\303\240 Implementate\\n\\n1. **Autenticazione & Spazio Condiviso (Household)**\\n   - **Codice Univoco a 6 caratteri** (es. `CASA01`) e pulsante rapido **\\\"Copia Link d\'Invito\\\"** con parametro URL automatico (`?code=...`).\\n   - Sincronizzazione in tempo reale (SSE - Server-Sent Events) tra smartphone e browser per vedere istantaneamente ogni m\\n<truncated 2052 bytes>\\nto (sistema)**.\\n   - **5 Tavolozze di Colore selezionabili**:\\n     - \360\237\214\277 *Verde Salvia / Fresh* (predefinito)\\n     - \360\237\217\272 *Terracotta / Warm*\\n     - \360\237\253\220 *Mirtillo / Deep Blue*\\n     - \360\237\245\221 *Avocado / Olive*\\n     - \360\237\252\250 *Monocromatico / Slate*\\n   - Salvataggio locale indipendente: ciascun partner pu\303\262 personalizzare il tema sul proprio smartphone.\\n\\n6. **PWA Mobile-First**\\n   - Web App Manifest (`manifest.json`), service worker, icone e layout ottimizzato per l\'uso ad una mano tra le corsie del supermercato.\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n{\"step_index\":66,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T10:04:41Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nDove posso vedere l\'applicazione?\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-17T03:04:41-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-w2op2gd7ig5avrhrpf6qqs-726438682148.europe-west2.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-w2op2gd7ig5avrhrpf6qqs-726438682148.europe-west2.run.app\\nUser Email: daniele.marra@buonarroti.tn.it\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\"}\n{\"step_index\":67,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-17T10:04:42Z\",\"input_tokens\":126082,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":555,\"content\":\"Puoi visualizzare e testare l\'applicazione direttamente a questi link:\\n\\n- **\360\237\224\227 Link di Sviluppo (Dev):**  \\n  [https://ais-dev-w2op2gd7ig5avrhrpf6qqs-726438682148.europe-west2.run.app](https://ais-dev-w2op2gd7ig5avrhrpf6qqs-726438682148.europe-west2.run.app)\\n\\n- **\360\237\214\220 Link Condivisibile (Preview):**  \\n  [https://ais-pre-w2op2gd7ig5avrhrpf6qqs-726438682148.europe-west2.run.app](https://ais-pre-w2op2gd7ig5avrhrpf6qqs-726438682148.europe-west2.run.app)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### \360\237\222\241 Come testarla subito anche da smartphone:\\n\\n<truncated 205 bytes>\\n`).\\n   - Sul secondo dispositivo (es. **Partner** \360\237\221\251\342\200\215\360\237\214\276), apri il link e inserisci il codice, oppure clicca su **\\\"Copia Link d\'Invito\\\"** per inviarglielo direttamente via WhatsApp/Telegram.\\n2. **Prova la spunta in tempo reale**: quando spunti un ingrediente nella Lista della Spesa al supermercato, apparir\303\240 barrato istantaneamente anche sull\'altro schermo!\\n3. **Installazione PWA**: da Safari (iOS) tocca *\\\"Condividi\\\" \342\206\222 \\\"Aggiungi alla schermata Home\\\"*, o da Chrome (Android) seleziona *\\\"Installa app\\\"*.\",\"thinking\":\"**Locating Application Instances**\\n\\nI\'ve got the user\'s question, translated it, and I\'m processing it now. The user\'s asking where they can access the application, and I\'ve identified two URLs. One is for development, the other is a shared instance. I\'m focusing on how best to present this information concisely.\\n\\n\\n\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n{\"step_index\":68,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:06:42Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nAll\'applicazione del menu voglio questa modifica: il calendario deve aprirsi e visualizzare le date e le settimane come quando apri il calendar. Non mi piace che venga visualizzato come Settimana 2026 . W43\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-20T10:06:42-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-w2op2gd7ig5avrhrpf6qqs-726438682148.europe-west2.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-w2op2gd7ig5avrhrpf6qqs-726438682148.europe-west2.run.app\\nUser Email: daniele.marra@buonarroti.tn.it\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\"}\n{\"step_index\":69,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:06:43Z\",\"input_tokens\":126999,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":465,\"thinking\":\"**Revising Calendar Display**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on refining the menu\'s calendar integration. The goal is to ensure the calendar opens in a standard view, similar to a typical calendar app. My aim is to eliminate the current display, which isn\'t preferred. I\'m prioritizing user experience.\\n\\n\\n**Improving Date Display**\\n\\nI\'m now shifting my attention to how dates are presented in the weekly view. The current \\\"Settimana 2026 \302\267 W42\\\" format isn\'t ideal, and the user prefers a more intuitive Italian date range like \\\"19 \342\200\223 25 Ottobre 2026\\\" or \\\"Questa settimana: 19 - 25 Ottobre.\\\" I am also focusing on ensuring an interactive calendar picker is integrated for date selection, similar to those found in Google Calendar or iOS Calendar. Each day card will also display the full date.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/data/initialData.ts\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"60\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking date helpers\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check date helpers in initialData.ts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":71,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:06:54Z\",\"input_tokens\":3950,\"cache_read_tokens\":124990,\"output_tokens\":2425,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Date Helpers**\\n\\nOkay, I\'m making good progress on those date helpers. My focus right now is on nailing down the `getWeekDates` function. I\'m aiming for a robust solution that accurately converts ISO week strings to a date range and provides all the necessary date-related data like the start, end, and individual days within the week. I\'m prioritizing accuracy and clarity in the data structures returned.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Date Calculations**\\n\\nI\'ve been drilling down into the date calculations, specifica\\n<truncated 297 bytes>\\nday\\\" flag. My goal is to ensure all data is correctly structured.\\n\\n\\n**Visualizing Calendar Components**\\n\\nI\'m now fully immersed in the UI components, focusing on replicating that familiar calendar interface. My goal is to create that month & year header with navigation, the day of week labels, and the grid of days. I\'m prioritizing the weekly highlight, today\'s date marker, and immediate week selection on any date click. I\'m also planning the shortcut buttons. I want this to feel intuitive and efficient.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Add robust ISO week to Date and Italian formatting helpers in initialData.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"40\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add date and week conversion utilities\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"export function getCurrentSeason(): Season {\\\\n  const month = new Date().getMonth(); // 0 = Jan, 9 = Oct\\\\n  if (month >= 2 && month <= 4) return \'spring\';\\\\n  if (month >= 5 && month <= 7) return \'summer\';\\\\n  if (month >= 8 && month <= 10) return \'autumn\';\\n<truncated 3561 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"20\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"export function getCurrentSeason(): Season {\\\\n  const month = new Date().getMonth(); // 0 = Jan, 9 = Oct\\\\n  if (month >= 2 && month <= 4) return \'spring\';\\\\n  if (month >= 5 && month <= 7) return \'summer\';\\\\n  if (month >= 8 && month <= 10) return \'autumn\';\\n<truncated 543 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/data/initialData.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Adding date helpers\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Add getWeekRangeDisplay and calendar helpers in initialData.ts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":73,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:07:13Z\",\"input_tokens\":3997,\"cache_read_tokens\":129063,\"output_tokens\":3172,\"thinking\":\"**Designing Calendar Picker**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on the Calendar Picker component, specifically the interactive monthly grid. I\'m thinking about including a month and year selector with back and forward buttons, much like the Google Calendar design. Next, I will flesh out the calendar UI more, along with functionality.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  X,\\\\n  ChevronLeft,\\\\n  ChevronRight,\\\\n  Calendar as CalendarIcon,\\\\n  Check,\\\\n  Sparkles,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { useHousehold } from \'../../context/HouseholdContext.tsx\';\\\\nimport { getCurrentW\\n<truncated 10329 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"CalendarPickerModal component displaying interactive month calendar grid with week-row highlighting, day selection and Italian localized dates\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/WeeklyMenu/CalendarPickerModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating CalendarPickerModal component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create CalendarPickerModal.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":75,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:07:38Z\",\"input_tokens\":3421,\"cache_read_tokens\":132992,\"output_tokens\":5431,\"thinking\":\"**Revising Weekly Menu Component**\\n\\nI\'m currently updating `WeeklyMenuView.tsx`. My focus is to replace the hardcoded date string with a clickable button featuring a calendar icon. This button should display the week\'s dates and provide access to a calendar for date selection.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  ChevronLeft,\\\\n  ChevronRight,\\\\n  Plus,\\\\n  Trash2,\\\\n  Users,\\\\n  User,\\\\n  Sparkles,\\\\n  ShoppingBag,\\\\n  RotateCcw,\\\\n  CalendarDays,\\\\n  Calendar as CalendarIcon,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { useHouseh\\n<truncated 18579 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update WeeklyMenuView to use natural date ranges (e.g. 19 \342\200\223 25 Ottobre 2026), full day dates (Luned\303\254 19 Ottobre), and interactive calendar picker modal\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/WeeklyMenu/WeeklyMenuView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating WeeklyMenuView component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update WeeklyMenuView.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":77,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:08:13Z\",\"input_tokens\":5755,\"cache_read_tokens\":136265,\"output_tokens\":135,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/Recipes/RecipesView.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"70\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking RecipesView for weekId references\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check RecipesView.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":79,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:08:19Z\",\"input_tokens\":3418,\"cache_read_tokens\":139844,\"output_tokens\":105,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/Recipes/RecipesView.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"430\",\"StartLine\":\"380\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking schedule recipe modal in RecipesView\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check lines 380-430 in RecipesView.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":81,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:08:31Z\",\"input_tokens\":3242,\"cache_read_tokens\":141093,\"output_tokens\":325,\"thinking\":\"**Updating the Recipe Display**\\n\\nI\'m currently working in `RecipesView.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m replacing the hardcoded text \\\"Scegli giorno e pasto nella settimana corrente ({activeWeekId})\\\" on line 381 with the result of `getWeekRangeDisplay(activeWeekId).label`. My aim is to show a user-friendly date range, improving the interface\'s clarity.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Import and use getWeekRangeDisplay in RecipesView\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"20\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Import getWeekRangeDisplay in RecipesView\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"import { Recipe, Season, DayKey, MealType } from \'../../types.ts\';\\\\nimport { SEASON_LABELS, getCurrentSeason, getWeekRangeDisplay } from \'../../data/initialData.ts\';\\\"\",\"StartLine\":\"17\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"import { Recipe, Season, DayKey, MealType } from \'../../types.ts\';\\\\nimport { SEASON_LABELS, getCurrentSeason } from \'../../data/initialData.ts\';\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/Recipes/RecipesView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating import in RecipesView\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Import getWeekRangeDisplay in RecipesView\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":83,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:08:54Z\",\"input_tokens\":2789,\"cache_read_tokens\":142267,\"output_tokens\":229,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Format week label with natural dates in RecipesView schedule modal\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"384\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Use getWeekRangeDisplay in schedule modal subtitle\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"                <p className=\\\\\\\"text-xs text-app-muted\\\\\\\">\\\\n                  Scegli giorno e pasto per la settimana: <strong className=\\\\\\\"text-app-main font-semibold\\\\\\\">{getWeekRangeDisplay(activeWeekId).label}</strong>\\\\n                </p>\\\"\",\"StartLine\":\"380\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"                <p className=\\\\\\\"text-xs text-app-muted\\\\\\\">\\\\n                  Scegli giorno e pasto nella settimana corrente ({activeWeekId})\\\\n                </p>\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/Recipes/RecipesView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating week label in schedule modal\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update schedule modal subtitle in RecipesView\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":85,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:09:00Z\",\"input_tokens\":2680,\"cache_read_tokens\":142905,\"output_tokens\":113,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/Recipes/AISuggestModal.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"180\",\"StartLine\":\"140\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking AISuggestModal for weekId displays\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check AISuggestModal.tsx lines 140-180\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":87,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:09:05Z\",\"input_tokens\":3214,\"cache_read_tokens\":143417,\"output_tokens\":109,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/Recipes/AISuggestModal.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"240\",\"StartLine\":\"200\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking destination labels in AISuggestModal\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check lines 200-240 in AISuggestModal.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":89,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:09:10Z\",\"input_tokens\":3185,\"cache_read_tokens\":144466,\"output_tokens\":307,\"thinking\":\"**Enhancing Date Display**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on `AISuggestModal.tsx`. I realized I can incorporate actual day dates within the Day dropdown using `getWeekDayDetails(activeWeekId)`. My next step is to update the component to reflect this enhancement, and I believe this will improve the user experience.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Add localized day dates to AISuggestModal day selector\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"16\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Import getWeekDayDetails in AISuggestModal\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"import { SeasonalAISuggestion, Season, DayKey, MealType, Recipe } from \'../../types.ts\';\\\\nimport { getCurrentSeason, SEASON_LABELS, getWeekDayDetails } from \'../../data/initialData.ts\';\\\"\",\"StartLine\":\"13\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"import { SeasonalAISuggestion, Season, DayKey, MealType, Recipe } from \'../../types.ts\';\\\\nimport { getCurrentSeason, SEASON_LABELS } from \'../../data/initialData.ts\';\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/Recipes/AISuggestModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating import in AISuggestModal\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Import getWeekDayDetails in AISuggestModal\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":91,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:09:21Z\",\"input_tokens\":2771,\"cache_read_tokens\":145566,\"output_tokens\":503,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Show real localized day dates in AISuggestModal day selector\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"235\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Show actual date in day dropdown\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"              <div>\\\\n                <span className=\\\\\\\"text-[11px] text-app-muted block mb-1\\\\\\\">Giorno:</span>\\\\n                <select\\\\n                  value={targetDay}\\\\n                  onChange={(e) => setTargetDay(e.target.value as DayKey)}\\\\n      \\n<truncated 574 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"216\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"              <div>\\\\n                <span className=\\\\\\\"text-[11px] text-app-muted block mb-1\\\\\\\">Giorno:</span>\\\\n                <select\\\\n                  value={targetDay}\\\\n                  onChange={(e) => setTargetDay(e.target.value as DayKey)}\\\\n      \\n<truncated 394 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/Recipes/AISuggestModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating day dropdown options in AISuggestModal\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update day select in AISuggestModal.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":93,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:09:28Z\",\"input_tokens\":3088,\"cache_read_tokens\":146174,\"output_tokens\":52,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"lint_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking linting after calendar update\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Run lint_applet\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":95,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:09:33Z\",\"input_tokens\":2289,\"cache_read_tokens\":147126,\"output_tokens\":46,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking build compilation\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Run compile_applet\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":97,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:09:51Z\",\"input_tokens\":2263,\"cache_read_tokens\":147280,\"output_tokens\":64,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"restart_dev_server\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Restarting dev server\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Restart dev server\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":99,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:09:55Z\",\"input_tokens\":2278,\"cache_read_tokens\":147408,\"output_tokens\":404,\"content\":\"Ho aggiornato la visualizzazione del calendario e delle settimane esattamente come richiesto:\\n\\n### \360\237\223\205 Cosa \303\250 cambiato:\\n\\n1. **Addio al formato tecnico (`Settimana 2026 \302\267 W43`)**:\\n   - Ora viene visualizzato il **periodo reale con date e mese in italiano**, ad esempio:  \\n     **`19 \342\200\223 25 Ottobre 2026`** (con etichetta verde **\\\"Oggi\\\"** per la settimana corrente).\\n\\n2. **Calendario Mensile Interattivo (\\\"stile Google Calendar\\\")**:\\n   - Toccando il pulsante delle date nella barra del menu, si apre una **vista\\n<truncated 353 bytes>\\n per saltare direttamente al rispettivo menu, oppure cliccare **\\\"Questa settimana (Oggi)\\\"** per tornare subito al menu attuale.\\n\\n3. **Date reali su ogni giorno del menu**:\\n   - Ciascuna scheda giornaliera non mostra pi\303\271 solo il nome del giorno, ma la data completa (es. **`Luned\303\254 19 Ottobre`**, **`Marted\303\254 20 Ottobre`**...).\\n   - Il giorno corrente \303\250 evidenziato con un bordo dedicato e il badge **\\\"Oggi\\\"**, rendendo immediato vedere cosa c\'\303\250 per pranzo e cena oggi.\\n\\nPuoi provarlo subito ricaricando l\'app!\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n{\"step_index\":100,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:12:02Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nOttimo non capisco a cosa serve il poter switchare come utente (partner o Daniele)\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-20T10:12:02-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-w2op2gd7ig5avrhrpf6qqs-726438682148.europe-west2.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-w2op2gd7ig5avrhrpf6qqs-726438682148.europe-west2.run.app\\nUser Email: daniele.marra@buonarroti.tn.it\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\"}\n{\"step_index\":101,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:12:03Z\",\"input_tokens\":150301,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":1069,\"content\":\"Il selettore serve principalmente perch\303\251 **l\'applicazione \303\250 pensata per due persone che usano ciascuna il proprio smartphone**:\\n\\n1. **Al supermercato (\\\"Solo la mia spesa\\\")**:\\n   - Nella lista della spesa c\'\303\250 il filtro **\\\"Solo la mia spesa\\\"**.\\n   - Se il tuo telefono \303\250 impostato su **Daniele**, vedrai solo i prodotti da comprare per i pasti *Insieme* e quelli per i tuoi pasti *Separati* (senza vedere le cose private che il partner deve comprare per s\303\251 nella sua abitazione).\\n\\n2. **Chi ha preso cosa in te\\n<truncated 499 bytes>\\nipalmente per **comodit\303\240 di test** (per consentirti di simulare entrambi i punti di vista anche provando l\'app dallo stesso computer o telefono).\\n\\nNella vita di tutti i giorni, **ciascuno imposta il proprio nome una volta sola sul proprio telefono**. \\n\\n\360\237\221\211 **Se preferisci una grafica pi\303\271 pulita**, posso togliere il pulsante di scambio dall\'intestazione e lasciarlo solo nella scheda **\\\"Spazio & Temi\\\"** come impostazione iniziale (*\\\"Questo smartphone appartiene a: Daniele / Partner\\\"*). Ti piacerebbe cos\303\254?\",\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing User Switch**\\n\\nI\'m now digging into the rationale behind the user-switching functionality, specifically why it was initially included in the specifications and implemented within the application. I\'m focusing on the \\\"partner\\\" and \\\"Daniele\\\" user roles. I will evaluate the feature in terms of its purpose.\\n\\n\\n**Clarifying Implementation Purpose**\\n\\nI\'m now revisiting the \\\"why\\\" of the user switcher. It appears the feature stems from the initial design, driven by the app\'s two-person household use case\\n<truncated 89 bytes>\\nice, and how dishes can be labelled for each user. It\'s key now to understand how we transitioned the prototype into a real implementation.\\n\\n\\n**Defining User Experience**\\n\\nI\'m now considering how the current app implementation contrasts with a single-login experience. The existing design aims to respect user preferences (theme) and shopping lists. This also includes the feature *\\\"Solo la mia spesa\\\"* (only my shopping). I am trying to resolve how we can enhance clarity on the benefits of single user mode.\\n\\n\\n\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\",\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":102,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:15:34Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nOK c\'\303\250 anche la possibilit\303\240 di mettere pi\303\271 case?\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-20T10:15:34-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-w2op2gd7ig5avrhrpf6qqs-726438682148.europe-west2.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-w2op2gd7ig5avrhrpf6qqs-726438682148.europe-west2.run.app\\nUser Email: daniele.marra@buonarroti.tn.it\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\"}\n{\"step_index\":103,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:15:34Z\",\"input_tokens\":3451,\"cache_read_tokens\":148353,\"output_tokens\":1101,\"thinking\":\"**Considering Multiple Homes**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on how to handle the possibility of a user managing multiple homes, as implied by the Italian question. The initial design centered on meal planning and management within a single home. I\'m reassessing to ensure the user can seamlessly handle multiple residences, avoiding any user experience limitations.\\n\\n\\n**Expanding Home Management**\\n\\nI\'m now thinking specifically about how the app should handle multiple homes. The core concept is that users need to define \\n<truncated 821 bytes>\\nusing on the code updates required by location-specific shopping lists. I\'ve found the `HouseholdContext` currently only handles a single household code, which is something I plan to adjust. I\'m expanding it to include an array of `savedHouseholds` in `localStorage`, and I\'ll add methods for switching and removing houses. Moreover, I\'m updating `MealSlot` and `ShoppingItem` to include optional location properties and defining the navigation, and how the user interface will reflect this new functionality.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/types.ts\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"90\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing types.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View types.ts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":105,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:15:50Z\",\"input_tokens\":2362,\"cache_read_tokens\":152088,\"output_tokens\":768,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Data Structures**\\n\\nI\'m currently updating the TypeScript definitions. I\'ve added a `location` property to the `MealSlot` type, specifying possible house locations. Similarly, I\'ve added a `targetHouse` property to `ShoppingItem`. I\'m also considering defining a `houses` type with ID, name, and icon properties to enhance data consistency.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Add location and house support to types.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"60\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add location to MealSlot and targetHouse to ShoppingItem\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"export interface MealSlot {\\\\n  type: MealSlotType;\\\\n  togetherDishes: Dish[];\\\\n  danieleDishes: Dish[];\\\\n  partnerDishes: Dish[];\\\\n  location?: \'casa_daniele\' | \'casa_partner\' | \'fuori\' | string;\\\\n  notes?: string;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nexport interface DayMeals {\\\\n  day\\n<truncated 509 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"27\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"export interface MealSlot {\\\\n  type: MealSlotType;\\\\n  togetherDishes: Dish[];\\\\n  danieleDishes: Dish[];\\\\n  partnerDishes: Dish[];\\\\n  notes?: string;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nexport interface DayMeals {\\\\n  dayKey: DayKey;\\\\n  dayLabel: string;\\\\n  pranzo: MealSlot;\\\\n  cena: Me\\n<truncated 374 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/types.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating types.ts with house and location support\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Add location and targetHouse to types.ts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":107,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:15:58Z\",\"input_tokens\":3286,\"cache_read_tokens\":152352,\"output_tokens\":487,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Add HouseDefinition and houses list to Household in types.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"105\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add HouseDefinition interface and saved households types\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"export interface HouseDefinition {\\\\n  id: string;\\\\n  name: string;\\\\n  icon: string;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nexport interface SavedHouseholdInfo {\\\\n  code: string;\\\\n  name: string;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nexport interface Household {\\\\n  code: string;\\\\n  name: string;\\\\n  users: HouseholdUsers\\n<truncated 429 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"84\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"export interface Household {\\\\n  code: string;\\\\n  name: string;\\\\n  users: HouseholdUsers;\\\\n  activeWeekId: string;\\\\n  menus: Record<string, WeekMenu>;\\\\n  shoppingList: ShoppingItem[];\\\\n  recipes: Recipe[];\\\\n  updatedAt: string;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nexport interface Seaso\\n<truncated 230 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/types.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating types.ts with houses definitions\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Add HouseDefinition and SavedHouseholdInfo in types.ts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":109,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:16:04Z\",\"input_tokens\":2989,\"cache_read_tokens\":153472,\"output_tokens\":212,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Initial Data**\\n\\nI\'m currently looking into the `src/data/initialData.ts` file, specifically the `createInitialHousehold` function with the code \'CASA01\'. My focus is now on the default `houses` array being created. I have added two houses, \'Casa Daniele\' and \'Casa Partner\', with their respective IDs and icons.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/data/initialData.ts\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"285\",\"StartLine\":\"240\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking createInitialHousehold in initialData.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check lines 240-285 in initialData.ts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":111,\"s