\"**Analyzing Shopping Data**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on how to best render shopping data in `ShoppingRow`. Specifically, I\'m examining how to display the target house information (like `casa_daniele`) when available. I\'m exploring the use of a conditional span to show this information, using the `item.targetHouse` value to determine visibility. I\'m aiming for a concise and visually muted representation using specific CSS classes.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Add target house selection and display in ShoppingListView\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"190\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add house selector to quick add in ShoppingListView\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"              <span className=\\\\\\\"text-app-muted text-[11px] font-medium mr-1\\\\\\\">\\\\n                Chi compra:\\\\n              </span>\\\\n              <button\\\\n                type=\\\\\\\"button\\\\\\\"\\\\n                onClick={() => setQuickAssignee(\'together\')}\\\\n     \\n<truncated 1745 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"148\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"              <span className=\\\\\\\"text-app-muted text-[11px] font-medium mr-1\\\\\\\">\\\\n                Chi compra:\\\\n              </span>\\\\n              <button\\\\n                type=\\\\\\\"button\\\\\\\"\\\\n                onClick={() => setQuickAssignee(\'together\')}\\\\n     \\n<truncated 1662 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/ShoppingList/ShoppingListView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Refining quick add bar in ShoppingListView\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update quick add in ShoppingListView.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":153,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:20:10Z\",\"input_tokens\":3709,\"cache_read_tokens\":199461,\"output_tokens\":58,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"lint_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking TypeScript linting\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Run lint_applet\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":155,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:20:16Z\",\"input_tokens\":2334,\"cache_read_tokens\":201035,\"output_tokens\":174,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Component Properties**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on the `WeeklyMenuView.tsx` file, specifically line 348. I\'m examining how the `onChange` event updates the `mealLocation` state. To understand its behavior, I\'m checking the `MealSlotCardProps` definition. My immediate goal is to understand what data is being passed around, and how it is ultimately being used.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/WeeklyMenu/WeeklyMenuView.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"330\",\"StartLine\":\"310\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking MealSlotCard props in WeeklyMenuView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check props in WeeklyMenuView.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":157,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:20:20Z\",\"input_tokens\":2815,\"cache_read_tokens\":201304,\"output_tokens\":348,\"thinking\":\"**Fixing Component\'s Props**\\n\\nI realized `mealType` was defined in the props of `MealSlotCard`, but I wasn\'t using it when destructuring. I\'ve corrected the destructuring on lines 319-328 of `WeeklyMenuView`.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Add mealType to destructuring of MealSlotCard props\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"328\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add mealType to MealSlotCard destructuring\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"const MealSlotCard: React.FC<MealSlotCardProps> = ({\\\\n  title,\\\\n  mealType,\\\\n  slot,\\\\n  dayKey,\\\\n  activeWeekId,\\\\n  onToggleType,\\\\n  onOpenAdd,\\\\n  onRemoveDish,\\\\n}) => {\\\\n  const { household, setMealLocation } = useHousehold();\\\"\",\"StartLine\":\"319\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"const MealSlotCard: React.FC<MealSlotCardProps> = ({\\\\n  title,\\\\n  slot,\\\\n  dayKey,\\\\n  activeWeekId,\\\\n  onToggleType,\\\\n  onOpenAdd,\\\\n  onRemoveDish,\\\\n}) => {\\\\n  const { household, setMealLocation } = useHousehold();\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/WeeklyMenu/WeeklyMenuView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Fixing destructuring in MealSlotCard\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Add mealType to MealSlotCard destructuring in WeeklyMenuView.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":159,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:20:28Z\",\"input_tokens\":2743,\"cache_read_tokens\":202031,\"output_tokens\":46,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"lint_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking linting after fix\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Run lint_applet\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":161,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:20:52Z\",\"input_tokens\":2280,\"cache_read_tokens\":202641,\"output_tokens\":58,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Testing compilation\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Run compile_applet\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":163,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:20:57Z\",\"input_tokens\":2273,\"cache_read_tokens\":202788,\"output_tokens\":53,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"restart_dev_server\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Restarting dev server\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Restart dev server\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":165,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:21:00Z\",\"input_tokens\":2265,\"cache_read_tokens\":202928,\"output_tokens\":438,\"content\":\"**S\303\254, assolutamente!** Ho implementato la gestione di **pi\303\271 case** su due livelli:\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 1. \360\237\217\240 Switcher rapido tra pi\303\271 Case / Spazi (in alto a sinistra)\\nOra in cima all\'app, toccando il nome della casa (es. **`\360\237\217\240 Casa Nostra \342\226\276`**), si apre un menu a tendina che ti permette di:\\n- **Passare in 1 click da una casa all\'altra** (es. *Casa Nostra*, *Casa Daniele*, *Casa Partner*, *Casa al Mare*, ecc.) senza dover reinserire il codice ogni volta.\\n- **\\\"+ Collega un\'altra Casa con codice\\\"**: per inserir\\n<truncated 460 bytes>\\ner**\\n  - \360\237\215\275\357\270\217 **Fuori / Ristorante**\\n- Nella scheda **\\\"Spazio & Case\\\"** puoi anche aggiungere altre abitazioni personalizzate (es. *\360\237\217\224\357\270\217 Casa Montagna*, *\360\237\217\226\357\270\217 Casa Vacanze*).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### \360\237\223\261 Profilo su questo smartphone:\\nIl pulsante di switch profilo \303\250 stato rimosso dalla barra superiore per non creare confusione: ora nella scheda **\\\"Spazio & Case\\\"** imposti una sola volta se quello smartphone appartiene a **Daniele** o al **Partner**. In alto a destra \303\250 rimasto solo un discreto badge informativo.\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n{\"step_index\":166,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:24:01Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nFacciamo che dipende dal numero di persone che sono associate a quella casa, quindi si potrebbe avere una sola persona associata, due persone associate o pi\303\271 persone associate\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-20T10:24:01-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-w2op2gd7ig5avrhrpf6qqs-726438682148.europe-west2.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-w2op2gd7ig5avrhrpf6qqs-726438682148.europe-west2.run.app\\nUser Email: daniele.marra@buonarroti.tn.it\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\"}\n{\"step_index\":167,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"CANCELED\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:24:01Z\",\"thinking\":\"**Defining the Variable**\\n\\nI\'m now thinking this should depend on the number of people associated with a household. It could be one person, two people, or multiple people associated. This variable will be fundamental and central.\\n\\n\\n\"}\n{\"step_index\":169,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:38:18Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nFacciamo che \\\"insieme/ separati\\\" dipende dal numero di persone che sono associate a quella casa, quindi si potrebbe avere una sola persona associata, due persone associate o pi\303\271 persone associate. Quindi nel caso c\'\303\250 una sola persona non compare \\\"insieme o separata\\\", nel caso di due persone puoi decidere se insieme o separate. Nel caso di pi\303\271 di due persone puoi creare degli insieme tipo se sono 3: 1 mangia sola e due insieme, nel caso sono 4 potrebbero: mangiare tutti soli, a due a due ma anche a tre e una sola e cos\303\254 via..\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-20T10:38:18-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-w2op2gd7ig5avrhrpf6qqs-726438682148.europe-west2.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-w2op2gd7ig5avrhrpf6qqs-726438682148.europe-west2.run.app\\nUser Email: daniele.marra@buonarroti.tn.it\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\"}\n{\"step_index\":170,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:38:18Z\",\"input_tokens\":206262,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":1458,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Association Dynamics**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on how the term \\\"together/separate\\\" should change based on the number of people associated with a residence. It seems that a simple one-to-one relationship is in order here, where the variable can take on unique states based on the size of the set. My intention is to come up with a formula.\\n\\n\\n**Elaborating Group Dynamics**\\n\\nI\'m now detailing how group dynamics shift with various household sizes. For a single occupant, the \\\"together/separate\\\" concept doesn\'\\n<truncated 1246 bytes>\\nmpatibility for older household data. It\'s time to check the files to see where data structures need updating. I\'m focusing on converting old `users` fields, which contained `daniele` and `partner`, into a dynamic `members` array, keeping the `users` property for fallback. In `MealSlot`, I\'m replacing individual dish fields with a `groups` array of `MealGroup` objects for more flexibility. There\'s a helper function planned to normalize old meal slots into the new `groups` structure during data migration.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/types.ts\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"115\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing types.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View types.ts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":172,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:38:39Z\",\"input_tokens\":3026,\"cache_read_tokens\":206653,\"output_tokens\":1437,\"thinking\":\"**Defining New Interfaces**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on defining the TypeScript interfaces for the application. Specifically, I\'ve outlined the `Person` and `MealGroup` types in `src/types.ts`. The `Person` interface includes `id`, `name`, and `avatar` properties, while `MealGroup` defines an `id` and an array of `memberIds`, which represent the people eating together. I\'m exploring how these structures will interact and evolve.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Data Structures**\\n\\nI\'ve been honing the data structures, specifically focusing on the `MealSlot`, `Household`, and `ShoppingItem` interfaces within `src/types.ts`. I\'m evolving the `MealSlot` structure to include dynamic grouping through `groups`, allowing flexible meal configurations. For `Household`, I\'m moving toward a dynamic `members` array. I\'m also changing `ShoppingItem` to allow a string for `assignee`, to handle single or multiple people.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"export type Season = \'spring\' | \'summer\' | \'autumn\' | \'winter\' | \'all_year\';\\\\n\\\\nexport type DepartmentCategory =\\\\n  | \'ortofrutta\'\\\\n  | \'macelleria_pescheria\'\\\\n  | \'latticini_freschi\'\\\\n  | \'dispensa_secco\'\\\\n  | \'surgelati\'\\\\n  | \'cura_casa_altro\';\\\\n\\\\nexpor\\n<truncated 2971 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Add Person, MealGroup, and dynamic members array to types.ts\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/types.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating types.ts with dynamic members and groups\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update types.ts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":174,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:38:51Z\",\"input_tokens\":3737,\"cache_read_tokens\":207696,\"output_tokens\":388,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Data Structure**\\n\\nI\'m currently examining the `src/data/initialData.ts` file. I\'ve begun to break down how meal slots are handled. The initial goal is to create a normalization helper function, `normalizeMealSlot`, which takes a `MealSlot` and a list of `Person` objects as input. My initial focus has been on how to handle the `slot.groups` property to streamline meal organization.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/data/initialData.ts\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"430\",\"StartLine\":\"395\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing createInitialHousehold in initialData.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View lines 395-430 in initialData.ts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":176,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:38:59Z\",\"input_tokens\":3214,\"cache_read_tokens\":209354,\"output_tokens\":180,\"thinking\":\"**Adding Member Data**\\n\\nI\'m currently working on incorporating member data and helper functions into `src/data/initialData.ts`. I\'m starting by defining `DEFAULT_MEMBERS`, including Daniele and Partner with their respective IDs, names, and avatars. The plan is to expand this list.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/data/initialData.ts\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"40\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing top of initialData.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View top of initialData.ts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":178,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:39:05Z\",\"input_tokens\":3295,\"cache_read_tokens\":210458,\"output_tokens\":745,\"thinking\":\"**Refining Data Structures**\\n\\nI\'m currently working on updating `src/data/initialData.ts`. I just imported `Person` and `MealGroup` from `../types.ts` and added the function `normalizeMealSlot(slot: MealSlot | undefined, members: Person[]): MealGroup[]`. The goal is to normalize meal slot data, providing a more structured representation for the app. I think this will greatly simplify later data operations.\\n\\n\\n**Implementing Logic**\\n\\nI\'ve just added the implementation for the `normalizeMealSlot` function. It handles several cases: empty slots, existing groups, single-member slots, and both legacy \'together\' and \'separate\' slots. The logic ensures each scenario results in normalized `MealGroup` data, crucial for consistent data processing throughout the application. I\'ve considered potential null values.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Add Person and MealGroup imports and normalizeMealSlot helper in initialData.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"4\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Import Person and MealGroup in initialData.ts\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"import { Household, Recipe, WeekMenu, Season, Person, MealGroup, MealSlot } from \'../types.ts\';\\\"\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"import { Household, Recipe, WeekMenu, Season } from \'../types.ts\';\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/data/initialData.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating imports in initialData.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Import Person and MealGroup in initialData.ts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":180,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:39:14Z\",\"input_tokens\":3215,\"cache_read_tokens\":211757,\"output_tokens\":143,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/data/initialData.ts\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"130\",\"StartLine\":\"110\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing initialData.ts lines 110-130\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View lines 110-130 in initialData.ts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":182,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:39:21Z\",\"input_tokens\":2827,\"cache_read_tokens\":212813,\"output_tokens\":725,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Add normalizeMealSlot helper in initialData.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"120\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add normalizeMealSlot function\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"  return result;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nexport function normalizeMealSlot(slot: MealSlot | undefined, members: Person[]): MealGroup[] {\\\\n  if (!slot) return [];\\\\n\\\\n  // Default fallback if members list is empty\\\\n  const activeMembers = members && members.length > 0 ? memb\\n<truncated 1607 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"117\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"  return result;\\\\n}\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/data/initialData.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Adding normalizeMealSlot to initialData.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Add normalizeMealSlot to initialData.ts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":184,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:39:28Z\",\"input_tokens\":3797,\"cache_read_tokens\":213447,\"output_tokens\":130,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/data/initialData.ts\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"480\",\"StartLine\":\"455\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing createInitialHousehold in initialData.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View lines 455-480 in initialData.ts\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":186,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:39:33Z\",\"input_tokens\":2813,\"cache_read_tokens\":215086,\"output_tokens\":313,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Add members array to createInitialHousehold in initialData.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"472\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add members array to Household initialization\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"    code,\\\\n    name: \'Casa Nostra\',\\\\n    members: [\\\\n      { id: \'daniele\', name: \'Daniele\', avatar: \'\360\237\221\250\342\200\215\360\237\215\263\' },\\\\n      { id: \'partner\', name: \'Partner\', avatar: \'\360\237\221\251\342\200\215\360\237\214\276\' },\\\\n    ],\\\\n    users: {\\\\n      daniele: { name: \'Daniele\', avatar: \'\360\237\221\250\\n<truncated 80 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"464\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"    code,\\\\n    name: \'Casa Nostra\',\\\\n    users: {\\\\n      daniele: { name: \'Daniele\', avatar: \'\360\237\221\250\342\200\215\360\237\215\263\' },\\\\n      partner: { name: \'Partner\', avatar: \'\360\237\221\251\342\200\215\360\237\214\276\' },\\\\n    },\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/data/initialData.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Adding members to createInitialHousehold\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Add members to createInitialHousehold in initialData.ts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":188,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:39:39Z\",\"input_tokens\":2791,\"cache_read_tokens\":215742,\"output_tokens\":484,\"thinking\":\"**Examining Household Context**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on the `HouseholdContext.tsx` file. My goal is to define the necessary context variables. I plan to provide a dynamic `members` array of `Person` objects, defaulting to a predefined array if `household.members` is not yet available. I need to make sure this default data is correctly integrated with the application flow.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Context Management Functions**\\n\\nI\'ve moved on to fleshing out the functions within `HouseholdContext.tsx`. I\'m detailing the member management methods now, including `addMember`, `updateMember`, and `removeMember`. Additionally, I\'m working on the meal slot group functions, such as `updateMealSlotGroups`, `setMealSlotMode`, `addDishToGroup`, and `removeDishFromGroup`. I am keeping backward compatibility by leaving `addDishToSlot` and `removeDishFromSlot` in place.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/context/HouseholdContext.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"90\",\"StartLine\":\"15\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing HouseholdContext.tsx interfaces\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View HouseholdContext.tsx interfaces\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":190,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:39:47Z\",\"input_tokens\":3993,\"cache_read_tokens\":216527,\"output_tokens\":8848,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Household Data**\\n\\nI\'m currently working on defining the structure of my `HouseholdContextValue` in `HouseholdContext.tsx`. I\'ve decided it needs an array for household members, `members: Person[]`. I\'m also including functions to add new members, `addMember`, and to update existing member details, `updateMember`. This should allow me to interact with the household members within the application.\\n\\n\\n**Expanding Household Functionality**\\n\\nI\'ve added several functions to the context. I\'ve included `removeMember`, `updateMealSlotGroups`, `setMealSlotMode`, `addDishToGroup`, and `removeDishFromGroup`. Now, I\'m checking how the `fetchHousehold` function populates the `members` array. I\'m focusing on handling cases where no members are initially present. I\'m converting the `daniele` and `partner` fields into the standard member format if `data.members` is empty or null.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { createContext, useContext, useState, useEffect, useCallback, useMemo } from \'react\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Household,\\\\n  ShoppingItem,\\\\n  Recipe,\\\\n  ColorTheme,\\\\n  DisplayMode,\\\\n  DayKey,\\\\n  MealType,\\\\n  MealSlot,\\\\n  Dish,\\\\n  MealSlotType,\\\\n  Assig\\n<truncated 29677 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Enhanced HouseholdContext with dynamic members management and multi-person sub-groupings for meals\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/context/HouseholdContext.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating HouseholdContext.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update HouseholdContext.tsx with dynamic members and meal groups\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":192,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:40:39Z\",\"input_tokens\":9292,\"cache_read_tokens\":220395,\"output_tokens\":3497,\"thinking\":\"**Designing the Modal**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on designing the Meal Group Manager modal, specifically for groups of three or more. My goal is to create a component, `MealGroupingModal.tsx`, that effectively manages meal assignments. It should clearly display the meal and day, like \\\"Luned\303\254 19 Ottobre \302\267 Pranzo\\\".\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { X, Users, User, Plus, Trash2, Check, Sparkles } from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { Person, MealGroup, DayKey, MealType } from \'../../types.ts\';\\\\n\\\\ninterface MealGroupingModalProps {\\\\n  isOpen: boolean;\\\\n  onC\\n<truncated 11676 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"MealGroupingModal component for organizing meal slots into sub-groups for 2, 3 or more members\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/WeeklyMenu/MealGroupingModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating MealGroupingModal component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create MealGroupingModal.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":194,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:41:05Z\",\"input_tokens\":3754,\"cache_read_tokens\":229620,\"output_tokens\":167,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/WeeklyMenu/AddDishModal.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"110\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing AddDishModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View AddDishModal.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":196,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:41:11Z\",\"input_tokens\":2127,\"cache_read_tokens\":233291,\"output_tokens\":678,\"thinking\":\"**Exploring Dish Context Options**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on the `AddDishModal.tsx` component. I\'m considering passing either a `groupId` directly or dynamically presenting a selection of available groups for dish assignment, via an array like `availableGroups`. My next step is to examine `WeeklyMenuView.tsx` to understand the current workflow and identify integration points.\\n\\n\\n**Analyzing View Display Logic**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining the rendering logic within `WeeklyMenuView.tsx`, specifically lines 320-450. I\'ve broken down how it handles different member counts. A single member has a simple display with a dish slot. Two members get an \\\"Together/Separate\\\" toggle, each option changing card displays. For larger groups, a dynamic badge/button shows group configurations, linking to a `MealGroupingModal` for easy adjustments, which displays group member names and dishes.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/WeeklyMenu/AddDishModal.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"140\",\"StartLine\":\"80\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking target selection in AddDishModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View lines 80-140 in AddDishModal.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":198,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:41:21Z\",\"input_tokens\":3967,\"cache_read_tokens\":233407,\"output_tokens\":3253,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Modal Props**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining the `AddDishModal.tsx` file, specifically the props needed. I\'m focusing on ensuring it receives `isOpen`, `onClose`, `dayKey`, and relevant contextual data like `dayLabel`, `mealType`, and available groups. I\'m also considering `defaultGroupId`.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { X, Plus, Sparkles, BookOpen, Clock, Check } from \'lucide-react\';\\\\nimport { useHousehold } from \'../../context/HouseholdContext.tsx\';\\\\nimport { Recipe, DayKey, MealType } from \'../../types.ts\';\\\\nimport { S\\n<truncated 11669 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update AddDishModal with dynamic group support based on number of people in the house\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/WeeklyMenu/AddDishModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating AddDishModal component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update AddDishModal.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":200,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:41:43Z\",\"input_tokens\":3500,\"cache_read_tokens\":237317,\"output_tokens\":7024,\"thinking\":\"**Rebuilding Weekly Menu**\\n\\nI\'m now focused on rebuilding `WeeklyMenuView.tsx`. My current focus is ensuring the view correctly handles the \\\"insieme/separati\\\" logic. Specifically, I\'m integrating logic to make this selection depend on the number of people associated with a household, allowing for scenarios with one, two, or multiple residents.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Group Logic**\\n\\nI\'m now refining the grouping logic within `MealSlotCard`. For single-member households, the \\\"Insieme/Separati\\\" option is removed, and the card shows their dishes with a \\\"+ Aggiungi piatto\\\" button. With two members, the toggle appears, switching between a shared card and two separate cards.  For larger households, I\'m working to make more complicated configurations of groups possible.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"Append\":\"false\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  ChevronLeft,\\\\n  ChevronRight,\\\\n  Plus,\\\\n  Trash2,\\\\n  Users,\\\\n  User,\\\\n  Sparkles,\\\\n  ShoppingBag,\\\\n  RotateCcw,\\\\n  CalendarDays,\\\\n  Calendar as CalendarIcon,\\\\n  SlidersHorizontal,\\\\n} from \'lucide-react\\n<truncated 23873 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Dynamic WeeklyMenuView supporting 1 person (no toggle), 2 people (together/separate), and 3+ people (sub-groups organizer)\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/WeeklyMenu/WeeklyMenuView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating WeeklyMenuView with dynamic person counts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update WeeklyMenuView.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":202,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:42:29Z\",\"input_tokens\":7400,\"cache_read_tokens\":240724,\"output_tokens\":258,\"thinking\":\"**Inspecting Housemember Management**\\n\\nI\'m currently looking at `src/components/Settings/SettingsView.tsx` to understand how house members are handled, specifically under \\\"Spazio & Case\\\" -> \\\"Persone Associate a questa Casa.\\\" It\'s showing the existing members like `\360\237\221\250\342\200\215\360\237\215\263 Daniele` and `\360\237\221\251\342\200\215\360\237\214\276 Partner`. My aim is to understand the UI elements involved in viewing these members.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/Settings/SettingsView.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"320\",\"StartLine\":\"240\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing user profiles in SettingsView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View lines 240-320 in SettingsView.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":204,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:42:35Z\",\"input_tokens\":4077,\"cache_read_tokens\":246013,\"output_tokens\":108,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/Settings/SettingsView.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"480\",\"StartLine\":\"380\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing profile section in SettingsView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View lines 380-480 in SettingsView.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":206,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:42:42Z\",\"input_tokens\":4062,\"cache_read_tokens\":247894,\"output_tokens\":359,\"thinking\":\"**Expanding User Settings**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining `SettingsView.tsx`, specifically lines 420-530. It initially focused solely on \\\"daniele\\\" and \\\"partner.\\\" Now, I\'m integrating the new requirement: \\\"Persone associate a questa casa (1, 2, o pi\303\271 persone).\\\" This means I need to display all members from the `members` array effectively.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/Settings/SettingsView.tsx\\\"\",\"ContentOffset\":\"0\",\"EndLine\":\"530\",\"StartLine\":\"470\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing profile forms in SettingsView.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View lines 470-530 in SettingsView.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":208,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-20T17:42:48Z\",\"input_tokens\":3772,\"cache_read_tokens\":249855,\"output_tokens\":2856,\"thinking\":\"**Refactoring User Display**\\n\\nI\'m currently working within `SettingsView.tsx` and planning a refactor. I\'m swapping out the static user list (`users: { daniele, partner }`) for a dynamic \\\"Persone Associate a questa Casa\\\" section. This will pull data from `members`. Each person\'s avatar, name, and activity badge will be displayed, and a button will be included for interaction.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Upgrade User Profiles section in SettingsView to dynamic multi-person manager\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"523\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Replace hardcoded 2-person section with dynamic members manager\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"      {/* 3. Persone Associate a questa Casa (1, 2, o pi\303\271 persone) */}\\\\n      <section className=\\\\\\\"bg-app-card rounded-2xl border border-app-subtle p-4 sm:p-6 shadow-xs space-y-4\\\\\\\">\\\\n        <div className=\\\\\\\"flex items-center justify-between border-b bor\\n<truncated 4913 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"419\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"      {/* 3. Profilo Utente & Nomi */}\\\\n      <section className=\\\\\\\"bg-app-card rounded-2xl border border-app-subtle p-4 sm:p-6 shadow-xs space-y-4\\\\\\\">\\\\n        <div className=\\\\\\\"flex items-center gap-2.5 border-b border-app-subtle pb-3\\\\\\\">\\\\n          <div cl\\n<truncated 4