  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Single Member Cases**\n\nI\'ve been drilling down on the scenario with a single member. Specifically, I\'ve noted that in the `WeeklyMenuView.tsx` file, the `DynamicMealSlotCard` component doesn\'t display the \"Insieme / Separati\" button when there\'s only one member. This is expected. The code comment explicitly states it.\n\n\n**Refining Single Member Display**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the UI behavior when there\'s a single member. The goal is to verify the display handles a single member slot properly and correctly. The current logic in `DynamicMealSlotCard` already prevents the \"Insieme / Separati\" button from showing. I\'ve confirmed that the UI doesn\'t incorrectly label the slot as \"Mangiano insieme\" when there\'s only one person. Now I am checking whether we can make it better by showing specific dishes of the user.\n\n\n**Exploring Grouping Scenarios**\n\nI\'m now diving into the complexities of handling more than two people associated with a household. For three or more members, the current design offers \"Insieme\" and \"Separati\" options but requires further refinement. I\'m focusing on the grouping modal, particularly `MealGroupingModal.tsx`, and how to make it more intuitive, especially for scenarios with three members. I\'m reviewing the current presets and options, beginning with the case of three members where the preset \"\360\237\221\253 Tutti Insieme (3)\" comes up.\n\n\n**Expanding Grouping Presets**\n\nI\'m now expanding the preset options for grouping within households of three or four members. For three, I\'m thinking of \"\360\237\224\200 Tutti Soli (1 + 1 + 1)\" and \"2 Insieme + 1 Solo\" with dynamic one-click combination buttons like `[Daniele & Partner] + [Marco]`. For four members, the presets would be \"\360\237\221\253 Tutti Insieme (4)\", \"\360\237\224\200 Tutti Soli (1 + 1 + 1 + 1)\", \"2 a 2\" (e.g., `[A, B] + [C, D]`), and \"3 Insieme + 1 Solo\". I am also planning an interactive drag/tap builder for more customized groupings.\n\n\n**Implementing Quick Grouping**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a streamlined grouping workflow. The goal is a quick, intuitive way to change group arrangements directly from the weekly menu. I\'m considering an inline dropdown or badge, like `[ \360\237\221\253 Tutti Insieme \342\226\276 ]` or `[ \360\237\247\251 2 Insieme + 1 Solo \342\226\276 ]`, offering instant preset options or quick access to the full organizer modal. I\'m exploring an efficient UI for switching between \"Tutti insieme,\" \"Tutti soli,\" or custom groups with minimal taps. I\'m also planning quick management features to associated household members.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_441910"
      name: "view_file"
