  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Meal Setup**\n\nI\'m currently focused on streamlining the meal setup process within `MealGroupingModal.tsx`. I\'m exploring one-click preset configurations that dynamically adjust based on the number of members. Specifically, I\'m thinking about offering options like \"Tutti Insieme\" and \"Tutti Soli\" for a group of three, as well as considering specific combinations for different group sizes. I\'m aiming for flexibility and user-friendliness.\n\n\n**Expanding Group Meal Options**\n\nI\'ve been expanding the meal setup presets. For a group of three, I\'ve got \"One Solo\" options with clear pill buttons. With four members, I\'m fleshing out \"Tutti Insieme\", \"Tutti Soli\", and options like \"A due a due\" and \"3 Insieme + 1 Solo\". I\'m also adding a new group editor. In it, you can click \"+ Nuovo Gruppo\" and click and tap people to move them.\n\n\n**Refining Meal Grouping Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the logic for meal grouping based on the number of people. If it\'s one person, I will show a clean header, title, location selector and dishes. For two people, the header will include \"Insieme\" or \"Separati\" options. For groups of three or more, I\'m introducing an interactive dropdown/button with a badge to show the meal configuration.\n\n\n**Implementing User Badges**\n\nI\'m working on `Navigation.tsx`, adding user count badges next to the house name. I\'m dynamically displaying `\360\237\221\244 1 persona`, `\360\237\221\253 2 persone`, or `\360\237\221\245 {N} persone` based on the number of members. Clicking the badge will provide a popup or open Settings for member editing. I\'ve also simplified the one-member case to avoid confusing \"switch\" terminology.\n\n\n**Expanding Meal Configurations**\n\nI\'m now building out meal configurations for different group sizes. I\'m focusing on modes for one, two, three, and four+ people, avoiding a \"together/separate\" toggle in the one-person mode. For two people, there\'s an \"Insieme / Separati\" toggle. Three-person groups will have options like \"1 solo + 2 insieme,\" \"tutti insieme,\" and \"tutti soli,\" extending to configurations for larger groups. I\'m prioritizing the addition of custom names, avatars, and the ability to remove members in meal setups.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Adjusting Shopping List View**\n\nI\'m updating `ShoppingListView.tsx`, replacing calls to specific user names with `members` from `useHousehold()`. I\'m adapting the assignee filter based on the number of members, hiding it for single-member households and displaying specific options (\"Tutti,\" \"Insieme,\" individual members) as group size increases. I\'m also adding assignee badges in the list, integrating member avatars and names.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
