    thinking: "**Considering User Access**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing user login via Google and allowing users to create their \"homes.\" I\'m figuring out how to let them invite others via a shared link, as requested. I\'m prioritizing user management and access control. This involves understanding how to structure user data and permissions efficiently.\n\n\n**Analyzing User Intent**\n\nI am now carefully analyzing the Italian text. The user\'s query highlights specific needs: Google login, house creation, link-based invitations, and account-linked houses. I\'m focusing on the \"Come faccio?\" part and interpreting it as a direct request for implementation guidance using the appropriate interactive tools, prioritizing Firebase Authentication and link-sharing capabilities. I\'m exploring the \"Agent Goals & Lifecycle\" guidelines to ensure I follow best practices.\n\n\n**Reviewing Firebase Integration**\n\nI\'ve hit a critical point: ignoring Firebase\'s setup instructions and resorting to hardcoded keys is a disastrous shortcut. The required UI interaction is non-negotiable! The Firebase tool instructions are very specific; I must first initiate the setup with `userConfirmedTermsAcceptedInUI: false`, wait for the user\'s response (accept or decline), and then proceed accordingly, not presume anything! This is a core part of the process.\n\n\n"
