  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Data Model**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the data model to accommodate multiple users, Google authentication, and user-created \"homes\" with shareable links. I need to consider how to represent users, their homes, and the relationships between them. Sharing permissions and how users are added to a \"home\" need careful planning.\n\n\n**Refining the User Model**\n\nI\'ve finalized the user model, incorporating Google authentication via `GoogleAuthProvider` and `signInWithPopup`, and `signOut`. User profiles will reside in Firestore at `/users/{userId}`, including `uid`, `email`, `displayName`, and `photoURL`. There\'s also a `households` array storing household codes. Non-logged-in users can preview a local demo house with a clear prompt to sign in for synchronization and sharing. I\'m focusing on incorporating a flexible structure for household data, including the `members` field to store info about people in the household.\n\n\n**Structuring Household Data**\n\nI\'m now focusing on structuring the household data. I\'ve decided on the following fields: `houses`: HouseDefinition[], `weeklyPlans`: Record<string, WeekPlan>, `shoppingList`: ShoppingItem[], `recipes`: Recipe[], `createdAt`: string, and `updatedAt`: string. I\'m also planning the direct share link for each household, `https://<domain>/?code=CASA01`. The UI will feature share buttons with various options, and automatic household addition for logged-in users via the share link, and a welcome screen for new users.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
