  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Firestore Rules**\n\nI\'m currently focused on ensuring the `firestore.rules` file is correctly structured. I\'m reviewing the essential global helpers and the overall structural components suggested for the skill. I\'m now implementing the necessary cloud.firestore rules.\n\n\n**Defining Access Rules**\n\nI\'ve just added the crucial security rules for the `/users` and `/households` collections. I\'m focusing on user authentication and ensuring data access adheres to the established `isOwner`, `isSignedIn`, and `isValidId` functions. Specifically, I\'m working to make sure these rule functions are implemented as intended.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_123479"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Append\":false, \"CodeContent\":\"rules_version = \'2\';\\nservice cloud.firestore {\\n  match /databases/{database}/documents {\\n    // Global Safety Net (default deny)\\n    match /{document=**} {\\n      allow read, write: if false;\\n    }\\n\\n    function incoming() { return request.resource.data; }\\n    function existing() { return resource.data; }\\n    function isSignedIn() { return request.auth != null; }\\n    function isOwner(userId) { return isSignedIn() && request.auth.uid == userId; }\\n    function isValidId(id) { return id is string && id.size() <= 128 && id.matches(\'^[a-zA-Z0-9_\\\\\\\\-]+$\'); }\\n\\n    // Users Collection\\n    match /users/{userId} {\\n      allow get: if isOwner(userId);\\n      allow list: if isOwner(userId);\\n      allow create: if isOwner(userId) && incoming().uid == request.auth.uid;\\n      allow update: if isOwner(userId) && incoming().uid == request.auth.uid;\\n      allow delete: if isOwner(userId);\\n    }\\n\\n    // Households Collection\\n    match /households/{householdCode} {\\n      // Allow get for signed in users looking up by code/link\\n      allow get: if isSignedIn() && isValidId(householdCode);\\n\\n      // Allow list queries only for houses owned by or containing this member\\n      allow list: if isSignedIn() && (\\n        resource.data.ownerUid == request.auth.uid ||\\n        (resource.data.memberUids is list && request.auth.uid in resource.data.memberUids)\\n      );\\n\\n      // Create: caller must be owner\\n      allow create: if isSignedIn() && isValidId(householdCode) && incoming().ownerUid == request.auth.uid;\\n\\n      // Update: caller must be owner or member or joining\\n      allow update: if isSignedIn() && isValidId(householdCode) && (\\n        resource.data.ownerUid == request.auth.uid ||\\n        (resource.data.memberUids is list && request.auth.uid in resource.data.memberUids) ||\\n        (request.resource.data.memberUids is list && request.auth.uid in request.resource.data.memberUids)\\n      );\\n\\n      // Delete: only owner can delete\\n      allow delete: if isSignedIn() && isValidId(householdCode) && resource.data.ownerUid == request.auth.uid;\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Write secure firestore.rules for users and collaborative households\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/firestore.rules\", \"toolAction\":\"Writing firestore.rules\", \"toolSummary\":\"Write firestore.rules\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
      original_name: "write_to_file"
