    thinking: "**Examining Context Integration**\n\nI\'m now diving into the integration of user authentication and Firestore within `HouseholdContext.tsx`. I\'m starting by defining the initial state for Google Auth. This includes `currentUser`, which will be either an `AppUser` or `null`, a loading flag called `isAuthLoading` for indicating authentication loading, and finally, a function `loginWithGoogle` for initiating the Google login process.\n\n\n**Implementing User Interactions**\n\nI\'ve just added a `logout` function to handle user logouts, returning a promise. I\'m now focusing on user profiles and household data within Firestore, specifically, the `/users/{uid}` document, ensuring it stores user details and their household memberships. Real-time listeners will keep the list of households in sync, and I\'ve planned to merge any locally saved household data upon login to prevent data loss.\n\n\n**Defining Household Management**\n\nI\'m now integrating logic for new household creation and invitation management. I\'ve configured automatic setting of the owner UID and initial member, alongside saving the new household to Firestore. I\'m focusing on crafting a shareable link that encodes the household code, enabling users to join with ease when logged in. Furthermore, I\'ve outlined the process for handling these links, including adding member UIDs to Firestore. If the user is offline, there\'s also a process for handling this case, which is critical to me.\n\n\n"
