    thinking: "**Refining Data Imports**\n\nI\'m currently working in `HouseholdContext.tsx`, integrating the necessary Firebase imports. I\'ve successfully incorporated the modules for authentication and firestore, specifically `auth`, `db`, and `signInWithGoogle` from `../firebase.ts`. I also imported `doc`, `getDoc`, and `setDoc` from `firebase/firestore`.\n\n\n**Integrating Firestore Updates**\n\nI\'ve integrated `updateDoc`, `onSnapshot`, and `arrayUnion` from `firebase/firestore`. In `HouseholdContextValue`, I\'ve expanded the typing to include the necessary updates, such as user information and a share modal state. I\'m also examining the helper function `cleanForFirestore` to make sure we scrub the right data for storage, and the `saveHouseholdState` function to be sure it saves correctly.\n\n\n**Implementing Data Syncing**\n\nI\'m now incorporating logic for syncing household data. I\'m focusing on the `saveHouseholdState` function, specifically how it interacts with both Firestore and the server API. I\'m looking at implementing the `cleanForFirestore` helper to ensure proper data formatting before saving. Also, I\'m working on the error handling for both the Firestore writes and the server fetch requests to improve the reliability of the system.\n\n\n**Adding Auth Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating logic for authentication state management using `onAuthStateChanged`. I\'m handling the user\'s data retrieval from Firebase and synchronizing their profile and saved households to Firestore. I\'m also ensuring the current household code is included, and handling cases where the user document doesn\'t yet exist in the database. I am also implementing a secondary fallback method, using fetch and an SSE listener.\n\n\n**Synchronizing Household Updates**\n\nI\'m now focusing on synchronizing household updates, specifically merging local and remote household data upon authentication. I\'m handling cases where a user document might not yet exist in Firestore, creating it if necessary. I\'m merging the local and remote household arrays, updating the user document with the merged list. I also added logic to fetch house names to ensure local and remote data are reconciled effectively. I\'m also ensuring the current household code is included, and handling cases where the user document doesn\'t yet exist in the database.\n\n\n**Formulating Household Creation**\n\nI\'m now formulating the logic for household creation. I\'m focusing on how the new household data is generated, including generating the code, creating the initial household, and handling the owner and member information. I\'m also dealing with how this new data is saved to both Firestore and the server API. I\'m handling the data save attempts to Firestore, including the data cleaning, and the POST request to the server, and the error handling for both.\n\n\n**Finalizing Household Logic**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on household joins and updates. I\'ve integrated `updateDoc` with `arrayUnion` to add new households to the user\'s document in Firestore. I am now working on the `joinHousehold` function, which first checks Firestore, with a fallback to the server if the document is not found. I\'m ensuring both options correctly handle adding the current user to the household and then saving to the database. I\'m focusing on managing the isLoading state throughout these asynchronous operations for smoother user experience.\n\n\n**Implementing Member Handling**\n\nI\'m now implementing the handling of household members. I am making sure to update `memberUids` and members when adding a user to a household. I also incorporated the logic for checking if the member already exists before adding to prevent duplicates. I\'m focusing on handling both cases, updating the household in Firestore, and then updating the user\'s profile with the new household code. I\'ve also implemented an update to the user\'s document in Firestore with the new household.\n\n\n"
