  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adding the Share Button**\n\nI\'ve just added the \"Condividi\" button within `Navigation.tsx`, specifically within lines 209-240. I integrated the button\'s functionality to open a share modal. This involves updating the UI for user interaction and setting the `setIsShareModalOpen` state. This will allow the user to share the app with others.\n\n\n**Implementing the \"Invite\" Button**\n\nI\'ve incorporated the \"Invita\" button within the UI for sharing capabilities. This involves styling with the provided classes for visual consistency and responsiveness across different devices. I\'ve also added the `Share2` icon and implemented the functionality to launch a share modal. This offers users a quick and accessible way to invite others via link or code.\n\n\n**Adding the Logout Button**\n\nI\'ve just added the logout button to the UI. I\'ve placed it next to the user\'s profile picture within the navigation bar. The button includes the `LogOut` icon and functionality to call the `logout()` function. I also styled it for consistency with other elements, incorporating hover effects and theming. The user can now logout via this button.\n\n\n**Adding Google Login**\n\nI\'ve integrated Google login. I\'ve created a button that triggers `loginWithGoogle()` when clicked. It\'s styled with relevant classes for visual consistency and responsiveness. I incorporated a Google icon within the button, to help the user identify the function. This should allow users to save and sync their homes using their Google account.\n\n\n"
