  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 2
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - User request: \"OK chiaro che senza fare l\'accesso l\'avatar \303\250 guest\"\n   - Core objective: When a user has NOT signed in via Google (unauthenticated / guest state), their avatar and identity indicator across the app (header navigation, role switcher, member slots) should clearly display as \"Guest\" / \"Ospite\" (e.g. icon `\360\237\221\244` or badge \"Ospite\") rather than hardcoding/falling back to \"Daniele\" or a specific member of the household.\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - Completed:\n     - Firebase Authentication (Google Sign-In) and Firestore database provisioned (`ai-studio-ideaflow-cdd35663-1681-4cae-907e-a5de32ff2712`, `firebase-applet-config.json`, `firebase-blueprint.json`, `firestore.rules`).\n     - `src/firebase.ts` implemented with GoogleAuthProvider and Firestore initialization.\n     - `HouseholdContext.tsx` updated with `user`, `isAuthLoading`, `loginWithGoogle`, `logout`, `isShareModalOpen`, Firestore dual sync.\n     - `ShareHouseholdModal.tsx` created for 1-click invite link copying and WhatsApp sharing.\n     - `Navigation.tsx` updated with Google Sign-in button, Invite button, and House Switcher.\n     - `SettingsView.tsx` updated with dedicated Google Account & Cloud Sync management.\n     - `App.tsx` updated with auto-join query parameter listener (`?code=...`) and toast notification.\n     - Build and linting (`tsc --noEmit` & `npm run build`) succeeded with zero errors.\n   - In progress:\n     - Updating the user avatar/identity display logic so unauthenticated users are clearly identified as \"Ospite\" / \"Guest\" instead of defaulting to `members[0]` (\"Daniele\" with `\360\237\221\250\342\200\215\360\237\215\263`).\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - In `src/components/Navigation.tsx` (lines 75-77):\n     ```tsx\n     const currentPerson = members.find((m) => m.id === currentRole) || members[0];\n     const currentUserName = currentPerson ? currentPerson.name : \'Daniele\';\n     const currentUserAvatar = currentPerson ? currentPerson.avatar : \'\360\237\221\250\342\200\215\360\237\215\263\';\n     ```\n     When `user === null` (not logged in with Google), if the user hasn\'t explicitly selected a household member role, it defaults to `Daniele`.\n   - In addition, in `Navigation.tsx` header:\n     - Line 222-230 displays the profile badge next to the Google Sign-in button. When not logged in, it shows `\360\237\221\250\342\200\215\360\237\215\263 Daniele`. Instead, if `!user`, it should indicate Guest / Ospite mode (e.g., `\360\237\221\244 Ospite` or clearly differentiate between the household members vs. the current Google account).\n   - In `SettingsView.tsx`: The persona selector (\"Chi sei?\") and the top user banner should also reflect Guest / Ospite state when not authenticated.\n\n4. **Active Context**\n   - Active Firestore database: `ai-studio-ideaflow-cdd35663-1681-4cae-907e-a5de32ff2712` (in `firebase-applet-config.json`).\n   - Dev server runs on port 3000.\n   - Files to modify:\n     - `src/components/Navigation.tsx`: Adjust `currentUserName` / `currentUserAvatar` and the profile pill when `!user`.\n     - `src/context/HouseholdContext.tsx`: Check default `currentRole` if unauthenticated.\n     - `src/components/Settings/SettingsView.tsx`: Ensure clarity between Google profile vs. household persona.\n\n5. **Next Steps**\n   - Step 1: In `src/components/Navigation.tsx`, update identity presentation:\n     - If `user` is logged in: display Google photo or initial, and `user.displayName`.\n     - If `!user`: display `\360\237\221\244 Ospite` (or `Guest`) on the profile pill with tooltip: \"Modalit\303\240 Ospite - Accedi con Google per sincronizzare le tue modifiche\".\n   - Step 2: In `SettingsView.tsx` (and `Navigation.tsx`), allow guest to view or pick a profile while making it obvious they are in unauthenticated/guest preview.\n   - Step 3: Run `lint_applet` and `compile_applet` to verify TypeScript builds cleanly without errors.\n   - Step 4: Respond concisely to user in Italian explaining that unauthenticated visitors are now displayed as \"Ospite / Guest\" (`\360\237\221\244`).\n\n6. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - No mock fallbacks for Firebase: use provisioned Firebase setup.\n   - Keep dual sync with local express backend for offline/fallback stability.\n   - Maintain Italian UI language consistent with the rest of the app.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_start: 216
    included_step_index_end: 335
    user_requests: "OK voglio adesso metterlo a disposizione di pi\303\271 utenti, che fanno il login con google si creano le loro case e inseriscono chi vogliono condividendo il link. Come faccio?"
    user_requests: "Firebase terms accepted, continue setting up database.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nuser_confirmed_in_ui: true\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
