  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Guest Display**\n\nI\'m focusing on how to best display the \"Guest\" option in the `SettingsView`. Specifically, I\'m thinking if the user isn\'t logged in, or if they\'re a guest, we should show a clear indicator like a \"Guest (Ospite)\" card. This could be placed prominently at the top, or integrated into the existing grid view for clarity.\n\n\n**Refining Guest Display**\n\nI\'ve been further refining the guest display option, and now I have a basic implementation to test. The new implementation features a prominent \"Guest (Ospite)\" card that clearly indicates the user\'s current role. It uses a conditional rendering strategy, displaying only when the user isn\'t logged in. I\'m keen to get feedback to further improve the implementation.\n\n\n**Implementing Guest Indicator**\n\nI\'ve made progress on the guest indicator. I\'m now integrating a new component into the `SettingsView` that displays \"Tap to use as Guest\" when the user is not logged in. I also added a checkmark indicator when the current role is \'guest\'. I\'m also updating the Google Account section to improve the display when the user is unauthenticated.\n\n\n**Developing Guest Profile**\n\nI\'m now working on the specifics of the guest profile display. I\'ve designed a \"Guest Profile (Ospite)\" section with a \"Not Connected\" badge. I\'ve also incorporated a descriptive paragraph that highlights the benefits of logging in with Google. It includes information on how being a guest limits account-specific features, but prompts users to login to save their houses on their personal account, and invite their families. I\'m focusing on making the call to action clear.\n\n\n"
