  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Envisioning Broader Access**\n\nI\'m considering the implications of broader access. The user wants to enable others to create their own \"house\" and manage their menu, similar to what\'s already in place. This prompts me to think about the architectural changes needed to support this. I\'m exploring how to generalize the existing functionality for a multi-tenant environment.\n\n\n**Analyzing User Onboarding**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the user onboarding flow, focusing on the initial experience. I\'m examining how new users interact with the application, particularly looking at the current state of `HouseholdContext.tsx` to understand the default settings and storage mechanisms, and the impact of the starting household, \"CASA01\". I\'m trying to identify where the current user experience may need refinement for a broader audience.\n\n\n**Refining New User Flow**\n\nI\'m now refining the new user flow. I see the need to improve the initial experience. Instead of defaulting to Daniele\'s \"CASA01,\" I am thinking of giving a more active choice for new users. I will offer clearer options like creating their own house, joining one, or exploring a demo. The Google login flow needs a revamp. I envision welcoming screens to facilitate house creation or connection when they first log in. I\'m focusing on simplicity and clarity.\n\n\n"
