  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining System Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `server.ts` file, and I\'m impressed by the combination of local JSON storage and real-time SSE. This local JSON store, combined with Firestore syncing, is a robust and interesting system architecture choice. I\'ll need to understand how the syncing occurs to see its effectiveness.\n\n\n**Analyzing User Flows**\n\nI\'m now investigating the user flow for a new house creation, specifically addressing the scenario where a user wants to create a unique menu. My focus is on understanding the onboarding process and the public accessibility, particularly concerning the UX gap for first-time users. The Cloud Run deployment makes sharing simple, but I\'m thinking about how the system handles the creation of these new houses, and how a user will know what to do!\n\n\n**Defining New User Onboarding**\n\nI\'m now detailing the new user onboarding flow. Without an existing household or a code, a clean \"Benvenuto\" modal will greet them with options: create a new house, join an existing one, or explore a demo. If a new user logs in via Google without saved houses, a similar prompt will appear. New houses will have a unique code.\n\n\n**Reviewing Invite Flow**\n\nI\'m now detailing the user flow after a house is created. I like how it creates a fresh, empty menu. It saves to Firestore and locally, then automatically opens the \"Condividi Casa\" modal with a unique link, QR code, and sharing options. I\'m focusing on the invite flow and the UX for new house creators, especially concerning the ease of sharing. The immediate access to sharing options is a key point to note.\n\n**Assessing Firestore Security**\n\nI\'m checking the Firestore security rules. I\'m focusing on the `households` collection. I\'m thinking about the implication of requiring `isSignedIn()` for `allow get` when someone accesses a link as a guest. I\'m curious if this means an unauthenticated guest cannot fetch `doc(db, \'households\', code)`. The scenario of guest access via a direct link is a key point to address.\n\n\n**Evaluating Security Implementation**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implications of the household code on security. It looks like anyone with the six-character code can read household data. I\'m considering allowing guest reads using `isValidId(householdCode)` in `firestore.rules`, enabling access via invite links. For writes, I\'m examining scenarios for both signed-in and unauthenticated users, thinking about how they are handled. I need to fully understand how updates sync through the local Express API.\n\n\n"
