  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Household Creation**\n\nI\'ve observed that a new household is initialized with the `createInitialHousehold(code)` function. It sets \"Casa Nostra\" as the name and populates it with members, \"Daniele\" and \"Partner\". Also, it sets the initial menus as well. It looks like it\'s a very simple and straightforward process, but needs to be explored more.\n\n\n**Clarifying User Requirements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on user needs during household creation. It\'s becoming clear that a new household should start with a clean slate: a user-defined name, unique code, the creator\'s identity, default locations, and a fresh menu and shopping list. The option to import sample recipes, rather than pre-populating with existing data, is crucial for user customization and privacy.\n\n\n**Defining New User Onboarding**\n\nI\'m now outlining the new user onboarding flow. A fresh household will have an empty weekly menu and shopping list. I\'m also including a collection of 15 seasonal recipes for inspiration. When a new visitor arrives, they\'ll see a welcome modal. The modal offers options: \"Create your Home,\" \"Join Existing Home,\" or \"Explore Demo.\" For sharing, users should share the app\'s link. They can then create a new home easily.\n\n\n**Implementing Household Invites**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implementation details of household invites. I\'m focusing on user independence within the household: each member will have their own independent weekly menu and shopping list. To facilitate this, I\'m integrating the functionality to invite others via a shareable link that directly links them to a specific household, ensuring real-time synchronization across devices. I\'m checking `src/data/initialData.ts` to figure out the needed changes. I\'m going to add a new function `createEmptyHousehold()` to handle new households.\n\n\n**Constructing Weekly Menu Framework**\n\nI\'m now establishing the structure for the weekly menu. I\'ve defined the framework with keys for each day and meal, `pranzo` and `cena`. The initial state for each meal is set to `type: \'together\'` and `groups: []`.  I\'m also including placeholders for future expansion. I\'m focusing on defining the initial menu values now.\n\n\n"
